{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc","id":868227,"title":"What do you want out of the Underworld, Abyssals, etc...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-18T23:46:11-07:00","id":868227,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What do you want out of the Underworld, Abyssals, etc...?","content":"Basically, all topics Underworld related that aren't completely new to this edition. What worked? What didn't? Any ideas on improvements?<br /> <br /> For me, I want an Underworld that matters. One that doesn't make sense for everyone to completely ignore except for the Deathlords, and those who later worry about the Deathlords. I think the Sidereals should have realized the problem there sometime after the Scarlet Empress took over and before Thorns, because it makes them look stupid if they didn't even consider the fact it might have some link to the Underworld. I want there to be a thousand kingdoms that had tinpot tyrants propped up by the Deathlords, as a way to hide themselves behind proxies as their power grew. I want a Stygia with smart rebels who don't try fighting face to face, but with trickery and hitting fast. Likely they should have some weapons and support from Sidereals funneling them weapons in the hopes of destabilizing some of the power of the Deathlords. Show us the different groups and give us reasons to care about the Dual Monarchy. Why have the Deathlords left them around? Is it because they're weak, or because they're a threat enough to even those who claim the title of Deathlord?<br /> <br /> And there's more, but at the heart of it, we need a better Underworld as a foundation for better Underworld related groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:57:18-07:00","id":868517,"title":"","content":"Frankly the Deathlords being Essence 10 super-Exalts didn't work, seeing how it caused an entire setting to be swallowed up in their gravity - shit, your post, where you want the Underworld to matter more beyond the Deathlords, manages to mention them more than a half-dozen times (I'm counting Thorns as a reference).<br /> <br /> That one bordello in the Labyrinth also <i>really</i> didn't work. Ugh.<br /> <br /> The casual references to soulforging ghosts sure didn't help to make the denizens of the Underworld feel important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:11:22-07:00","id":868802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=868517#post868517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one bordello in the Labyrinth also <i>really</i> didn't work. Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motion to disagree: having places like that bordello, the nigh-impenetrable prison-hekacthonkire, and casual references to the Labyrinth and the Underworld saturated with hellish and heavenly Afterlives from the various cultures in Creation felt refreshing. The land of the dead should be morphic based on the conceptions, and predilections, of the Dead in ways that would mirror how raksha influence the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The problem was that we spent most of the Underworld focusing on how ridiculously powerful the Deathlords are (to the point that everything felt like They owned it, why bother making anything else) and how much it sucked in the more hellish and boring portions of the Underworld (which made the Underworld feel grey or overly morose, why bother visiting). Most of the ghosts there are either trying to recapture something positive from life, or are actively conditioned to seek out the Happy Hunting Grounds/Longhouse Of Valhalla/Honored Seat Of The Ancestors; the afterlife is seen as a place people should aspire to go, and a place that sacrifice will make better for your lost family members (and eventually, you). Where's the great houses of wine and merry warriors? Where's the men and women sitting on clouds with harps, watching their lesser brethren/sisters roasting alive in self-inflicted hellscapes?<br /> <br /> Where's the part where First and Forsaken Lion has been in a two-hundred year prolonged siege with the Revered Ancestors of Lhasa as the living spin prayer-mills and wash mandalas away with sacrificial blood to preserve their grandfathers' conception of Heaven/Nirvana? What happens when an Abyssal from Halta enters Linowan-based Underworld, or a former Hindu-alike has to take a shortcut through Baptist Hell to get a message to his contact in Daoist Limbo?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:14:41-07:00","id":868807,"title":"","content":"I want a bunch of extinct civilizations that still persist because of their people's ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:23:18-07:00","id":868816,"title":"","content":"Someone I know (won't say who, it's personal) once confided in me that the bit of media that resonated the most with them was Angel - specifically the story of a man who was one of the damned, who nonetheless walked the Earth and tried to do good.<br /> <br /> It's not really a story that finds much fertile ground with me, because I've never felt like that. But I would like support for that sort of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:37:55-07:00","id":868831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=868802#post868802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Motion to disagree</div> </div> </div> </div>Motion denied, even allowing for the House of Succulent Tears' ideology that the rape of rapists = justice as appropriate Spectre logic the whole thing is rooted firmly in the notion that rape is an act commited by a man upon a woman. It's not just distasteful it's &quot;was this even written with the Exalted setting in mind?&quot; and I'm really vague on how the PCs were supposed to interact with it. There's like one plot hook I saw with it and that involved the Lover Clad using it to punish minions... she hardly needs to outsource for this kind of thing!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T15:48:44-07:00","id":868842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=868816#post868816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone I know (won't say who, it's personal) once confided in me that the bit of media that resonated the most with them was Angel - specifically the story of a man who was one of the damned, who nonetheless walked the Earth and tried to do good.<br /> <br /> It's not really a story that finds much fertile ground with me, because I've never felt like that. But I would like support for that sort of story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Along those lines, I once said that to me, I wanted Solars to be the big damn heroes (as in classic term, for better or worse) who go out seeking to make their dreams into reality. They're people who WANT and will move heaven and earth to get it. Abyssals I wanted to be the sort of person who said &quot;I couldn't live with myself if I stood by and did nothing, said nothing.&quot; People who have something gnawing at them that won't let them rest, even by dying. I want them driven not by want, but by a need bordering on madness. If I were going to describe it mechanically... if Solars favor Principles as their Intimacies, then Abyssals favor Ties of passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:03:25-07:00","id":868855,"title":"","content":"I recently went back and reread some of the 1ed Abyssal-book, and something that I didn't notice reading it some years ago, but that I really think that book does a good job at capturing, at parts, is the baseness of existence.<br /> <br /> The occasional focus on, and/or description of bodily functions, ( /body horror, nakedness etc.) and coldness* (discomforts) of life, and the body/mortality as something unwanted, something less than fantastic, and maybe even a prison, really resonates with the anti-life kaos-gnosticistic satanism themes that I feel the Abyssals incorporate so well. I would really like to see that still present, in parts at least, of the Abyssal write down.<br /> <br /> In the larger-than-life genre mainly incorporated by the Solars stories, where the dreams and aspirations of the characters soars high and the players symbolise the hope for a better future, where the possibilities for a brighter tomorrow is ever-present,<br /> Focusing on the body, the baseness of life, the uncomfortable truths and inevitables of existence, becomes a questioning of whether life is actually at all that great, and a perfect contrasting genre to that of the Solars, further strengthening the Core Conflict of the Solars as symbols for the Highest, the highet hopes we all can strive for, and the Abyssals, as symbols for the Lowest, the darkest depths we all can sink to.<br /> I Love It!<br /> More Abyssals. give me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> *The part with Prince waking up from having been dream-visited by the Lover in the intro story, was the part that really hit home for me. other good examples are the genitals being present in The Bishops true form, the penis-clutch on the Physicians table in the ilustration accompanying his chapter fiction, the juxtaposition of nakedness and chains of the Oblivion-priestess.<br /> **Temple of the Black Light philosophy-stuff<br /> <br /> Edit: Of course, I want more than just this. I want all splats to incorporate several fitting thematics, so that there is a breadth for players and GMs to choose the things they prefer, that speaks to them the most about that certain splat. But I want this themaic to at least be/stay present in some way/part of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","user":"Kim","date":". 04-19-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:03:46-07:00","id":868856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=868807#post868807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a bunch of extinct civilizations that still persist because of their people's ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you hate your players, run a First Age game and then reveal at the end of the game that all the characters are actually ghosts. It's actually the Age of Sorrows and the characters are just playing out their sad little dramas. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T17:10:50-07:00","id":868905,"title":"","content":"I want Abyssals that can be good, evil, or somewhere in between and be compelling anywhere on the spectrum.<br /> <br /> I want an Underworld that I would actually want to visit, because the rewards of going there potentially outweigh the risks and general inconvenience.<br /> <br /> I want Deathlords that could really be respected leader-figures, albeit not of the kind that history will remember fondly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T18:48:39-07:00","id":868978,"title":"","content":"An underworld that has interesting societies and locations beyond Stygia is the main thing I want.<br /> <br /> Abyssals that are playable in a mixed group would be the second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T19:26:37-07:00","id":869005,"title":"","content":"Lots of great ideas, please, keep them coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T19:38:16-07:00","id":869017,"title":"","content":"Quoting myself:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=868636#post868636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) divorce the Deathlords from being straight-up servants of the Neverborn and universally interested in promoting Oblivion (in theory). I think it allows them more freedom if they have merely, say, been touched by the essence of the Neverborn, or plundered their tombs for power, and were changed in the process, each one affected to different degrees. So you can have one who declares themselves enemies to oblivion and the Neverborn, one who does believe in the former to a similar degree as Nephwracks, one who's just interested in building up and preserving their realm in the Underworld, one who wishes to develop and build up the Underworld, one whose interests lie in covering all of Creation in Shadowlands...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lately, one of the things I've been thinking I want out of the new Underworld the most is some real diversity and ambiguity in the motives and methods of the Deathlords. A way in which this is more easily enabled in comparison to the previous edition is by making their place in the setting ortogonal to or mostly detached from the Neverborn, and elaborating on their characters in a way that they can be interesting or even sympathetic as individuals.<br /> <br /> There's more (that's already been named), but I really want to see much richer and dynamic Deathlords than before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-19-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:45:43-07:00","id":869068,"title":"","content":"Before reading anything posted in this thread:<br /> <br /> * Oblivion is a state of non-being. It is not a force that actively destroys anything, but rather the condition of having been completely destroyed. Oblivion is what what happens when you Ghost-Eating Technique a god; the god is obliterated.<br /> <br /> * Oblivion does not whisper or drive creatures mad -- the Neverborn do.<br /> <br /> * The Deathlords and Abyssal Exalted do not draw power from Oblivion, because Oblivion is not a creature or force. It is &quot;nothing&quot; to the extent that Elsewhere is &quot;no where&quot;, and while Exalted have Charms that interact with Elsewhere, there will never be anything that draws power from &quot;the state of being no where&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Any power that needs to be begged, borrowed, or burgled should come from the Neverborn or powerful ghosts. This includes powerful ghosts who have Neverborn-derived power, such as the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> * Ghosts struggle to avoid the loss of self which would plunge them into Lethe and reincarnation; they do not struggle against Oblivion unless assaulted by a force that seeks to obliterate them.<br /> <br /> * Abyssal Exalted have the power to Obliterate creatures because all of the Exalted do; they were MEANT to kill things Deader Than Dead, in order to have a chance at killing things which could not die.<br /> <br /> * Both the Abyssal Exalted AND the readers need to care about the denizens of the Underworld as if they were people, and this is rather hollow if ghosts just AREN'T people. If necessary, be unclear and ambiguous about whether ghosts are people or merely the mindless, endlessly-repeating echoes of dead people. If the only people in the Underworld are 100ish Deathknights, will many players or even many Deathknights care to dwell there for long?<br /> <br /> * The Charms of the Abyssal Exalted should reflect undeath in general -- memory; the stubborn refusal to forget, forgive, forsake, or pass on; stagnation; repetition; leeching life and material goods from the living world and its creatures. They should also reflect undeath in variety -- Charms that would be at home in the most hellish or heavenly of afterlives, though seldom without an unhealthy twist to remind you that this is an unnatural state of being for Creation.<br /> <br /> * As a sub-note to the above, the afterlives that Abyssals reflect should include the elemental environments -- hells of fire, hells of ice, hells of poisonous swamps or drowning depths or deserts of endless thirst.<br /> <br /> * The Deathlords should be archetypical embodiments of the things the Abyssals represent. Where an Abyssal can mix and match to taste, each Deathlord should be a two-dimensional caricature of a particular field of power of which Abyssals can learn.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T22:19:02-07:00","id":869114,"title":"","content":"Actually, at least in 2e, there was clarification (perhaps via contrast with its Abyssal Mirror? Might've been &quot;stealth errata&quot; at the time) that a Ghost-Eaten spirit is forced through Lethe, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-20-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T00:47:37-07:00","id":869162,"title":"","content":"I personally kinda hope resonance sticks around in some form, just because, for me, it was actually what made me really excited to try playing a 'good' abyssal. I know it gets flak for being restrictive at times but as someone who struggles with chronic depression and was struggling with it at the time i first found the game, the concept of playing someone trying to enjoy life, care about others, and be heroic despite this palpable manifestation of doom that was always trying to throw a wrench in their plans or keep them down was very powerful to me. Its always felt like one of the greater heroic arcs you can play in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":4416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","user":"Heedra","date":". 04-20-2016, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:00:23-07:00","id":869249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=869114#post869114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, at least in 2e, there was clarification (perhaps via contrast with its Abyssal Mirror? Might've been &quot;stealth errata&quot; at the time) that a Ghost-Eaten spirit is forced through Lethe, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind, but if so, I hope the same applies to ghosts.<br /> <br /> It would also be great if there's clarificaiton on whether using Ghost-Eating Technique on a living human forces their higher soul into Lethe without the chance to become a ghost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:11:39-07:00","id":869256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=869249#post869249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind, but if so, I hope the same applies to ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are spirits, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:21:42-07:00","id":869266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=869068#post869068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before reading anything posted in this thread:<br /> <br /> * Oblivion is a state of non-being. It is not a force that actively destroys anything, but rather the condition of having been completely destroyed. Oblivion is what what happens when you Ghost-Eating Technique a god; the god is obliterated.<br /> <br /> * Oblivion does not whisper or drive creatures mad -- the Neverborn do.<br /> <br /> * The Deathlords and Abyssal Exalted do not draw power from Oblivion, because Oblivion is not a creature or force. It is &quot;nothing&quot; to the extent that Elsewhere is &quot;no where&quot;, and while Exalted have Charms that interact with Elsewhere, there will never be anything that draws power from &quot;the state of being no where&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Any power that needs to be begged, borrowed, or burgled should come from the Neverborn or powerful ghosts. This includes powerful ghosts who have Neverborn-derived power, such as the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> * Ghosts struggle to avoid the loss of self which would plunge them into Lethe and reincarnation; they do not struggle against Oblivion unless assaulted by a force that seeks to obliterate them.<br /> <br /> * Abyssal Exalted have the power to Obliterate creatures because all of the Exalted do; they were MEANT to kill things Deader Than Dead, in order to have a chance at killing things which could not die.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like these ideas. I've always loved the Underworld, especially in 1st Edition (Wraith the Oblivion much? :P) and these would be a really nice addition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:35:33-07:00","id":885426,"title":"","content":"I finally went to see <i>Kung Fu Panda 3</i>, and now I want part of the Underworld to be like &quot;the Spirit World&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the ancient past, two brothers in arms turned against each other, and Master Oogwei was forced to kill Kai. But Kai's greedy spirit would not rest, and his ghost used what he had learned of harnessing and stealing Chi to track down, defeat, and absorb other mighty ghosts.<br /> <br /> In the mortal realm, Master Oogwei reaches the end of his natural life, and uses his understanding of Chi to transcend Lethe, becoming a special kind of ghost who lacks the vibrancy of life but whom can continue to guide and assist the living without falling prey to restless passions that would turn him into an antagonistic force.<br /> <br /> Or else the old turtle never really was going to die at all, and he just bodily up and left the mortal world to take a vacation in Ghost Town so that Master Shifu and Po would figure out how to solve their own problems.<br /> <br /> Either way, the ethereally beautiful Spirit Realm in which Kai battles Oogwei and later Po is definitely the sort of haunting, peaceful, place that the Underworld can be. Empty, abandoned, ruined structures of former grandness which seem to recall a time which no longer exists. Very characteristic of the Underworld's themes of remembering things which are wrecked and gone forever, but with a somber and soft quality rather than a frenzied bitterness or sullen resignation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Po's Wu Shi Finger Hold sends the living into the world of the dead while still alive, judging by how he could use it on himself. Which also lends weight to the idea that Oowgei used a similar trick for himself in the first movie.<br /> <br /> Also, that's totally now a plot hook for Tai Lung to eventually return in a fourth movie, though probably not as the antagonist. or at least not the primary one. He'll either be serving as a minion for the next villain from the Spirit Realm or else he'll be the one to warn Po of the new danger.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:10:31-07:00","id":885686,"title":"","content":"I mainly just want the Underworld to be a place where I could run a full campaign for a party of any type of Exalted and have it be cool. (Obviously, &quot;the Lunars game that takes place entirely in the Underworld&quot; is going to be super weird, but so long as it's <i>good</i> I'm happy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:43:35-07:00","id":885716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885686#post885686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mainly just want the Underworld to be a place where I could run a full campaign for a party of any type of Exalted and have it be cool. (Obviously, &quot;the Lunars game that takes place entirely in the Underworld&quot; is going to be super weird, but so long as it's <i>good</i> I'm happy.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't you do that?<br /> <br /> Edit: What about it, specifically, is not cool enough for you to game in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:54:53-07:00","id":885723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885716#post885716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't you do that?<br /> <br /> Edit: What about it, specifically, is not cool enough for you to game in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, are there any PEOPLE in the Underworld, or just the echoes of people who died? Echoes that endlessly repeat certain actions and who can only feel and think just enough manic passions that they can qualify for two-dimensional characters at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:55:57-07:00","id":885724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885716#post885716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't you do that?<br /> <br /> Edit: What about it, specifically, is not cool enough for you to game in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's generally accepted by most of the fan community that as it's been presented before, the Exalted Underworld is bad... I've had so many people say they didn't imagine ANYTHING cool could come from or exist there. It's kinda like how there were never the first two chapters written for the Infernals book. It's not that the Underworld HAS to be boring, it's that it's always BEEN written that way previously. Which is what most people want changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:30:01-07:00","id":885855,"title":"","content":"I liked Stygia.<br /> Not much else interesting going on in the Underworld though. No interesting societies or stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:49:04-07:00","id":885869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885716#post885716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why can't you do that?<br /> <br /> Edit: What about it, specifically, is not cool enough for you to game in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, previously the game was set up to cut off as many as your resources as possible just for being in the Underworld, which severely limited your ability to actually engage with the game's system. The underworld was also 99% undefined and not terribly inspiring -- aside from a couple of cool core cities, the underworld didn't have a lot to actually sell it as a campaign setting, or for that matter as an actual place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:31:48-07:00","id":885893,"title":"","content":"I haven't read much about the 1E-2E Underworld, so I apologize in advance if I mention something that's actually already there... <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I'd like an Underworld that isn't just all about the Deathlords.</li> <li>And Deathlords that aren't 5 months (or was it 5 years) from annihilating Creation in 13 different ways, or worse, could do it at any time and inexplicably haven't bothered yet. I'd like to feel more comfortable regarding anything other than &quot;Saving the World, Oh My Gods, It's an Emergency, Drop Everything!!!!&quot; campaigns as relevant and important.</li> <li>I want Sidereals who have enough brain cells to seriously consider the Underworld a major threat, realize that the Contagion was connected to it, investigate the Underworld enough to notice that something was stirring, and have <i>plans for how to help the Dragon-Blooded combat it</i>, not being completely blindsided by Thorns because &quot;Herp derp, it was outside of Fate, like, it never occured to me that anything could come from there!&quot; In 2E and especially 1E this made them look very stupid.</li> <li>^ This should mean Sidereals have spies and agents and plots in the Underworld, not just very recently in response to Thorns but for at least the last few centuries of the Second Age. And double-agents. And webs of contacts. The Solars had actual foreign relations with the Dual Monarchy, let's see how the Sidereals tried to maintain or change Exalted relationships with the dead after the Usurpation.</li> <li>Does the mere existence of ghosts really further Oblivion no matter what those ghosts actually do with their afterlives? Maybe it shouldn't. Maybe it should be ambiguous whether or not it's a good thing that humans now have an afterlife option and a way to continue their memories and help their descendants, that wasn't available before, instead of it always being a tool of the Neverborn and Deathlords. It's unnatural... but so is Exaltation. Maybe when it comes to some things, what the Primordials set up sucks?</li> <li>I'd like an Underworld that's full of weird, terrible, inexplicable, creepy phenomena that can't even be lumped together as hekatonkhires, because it's a giant abscess that wasn't supposed to exist, in a hole ripped in reality. (And said reality was already full of weird, inexplicable shit.)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Fortunately I'm pretty sure #1 and #2 are already confirmed to be happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T22:20:42-07:00","id":885966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=868831#post868831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really vague on how the PCs were supposed to interact with it. There's like one plot hook I saw with it and that involved the Lover Clad using it to punish minions... she hardly needs to outsource for this kind of thing!</div> </div> </div> </div>How Ms. Clad in Raiment of Tears utilizes her resources is nobody's business but her own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T05:45:39-07:00","id":886136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885716#post885716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't you do that?<br /> <br /> Edit: What about it, specifically, is not cool enough for you to game in?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s some fairly fundamental baggage attached to the idea of if ghosts should exist or if they\u2019re even really people anymore coupled with a tendency to have undead kingdoms that could work just as easily or better as living ones.<br /> <br /> For example, the dual kingdom of Hanau and Tyoka is pretty cool because its throne is shared by Princess Annuaski and her ancestor Queen Defiance-in-Shadow two monarchs from different points in history with very different styles of rule.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this dual ruler dynamic is expressed as a Summer/Winter Court where Annuaski frequently wastes all the resources leaving Defiance-in-Shadow's half of the year to be a time of austerity and hardship that sucks and if these were two spirits ruling over a mortal population most of my characters would be all over deposing Annuaski yesterday but... when you give it a moments thought, food, warmth and shelter are strictly comfort things for a ghost and if half a year of excess lets them forget that they're stuck in limbo I'm not going to judge, <i>however</i> I don't think we were supposed to look at it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:36:25-07:00","id":886164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885893#post885893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Sidereals who have enough brain cells to seriously consider the Underworld a major threat\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally not much rather have an entire realm of existence categorized as &quot;a major threat.&quot; At least no moreso than Prasad or Yu-Shan or the Realm is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885893#post885893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026realize that the Contagion was connected to it\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says it is? Who says it has to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885893#post885893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026investigate the Underworld enough to notice that something was stirring\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>What? What's stirring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:45:52-07:00","id":886172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885869#post885869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, previously the game was set up to cut off as many as your resources as possible just for being in the Underworld, which severely limited your ability to actually engage with the game's system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it should do that.<br /> <br /> The Underworld should not, in my opinion, be a place you can just walk into for a day trip. Even if they aren't going to go the full &quot;the fact that the Underworld exists at all is a fucked-up mistake created by the Exalted murdering things that shouldn't have been capable of being murdered&quot; on it, it shouldn't be the kind of place that the quick, even the Exalted, can easily penetrate deep into.<br /> <br /> Because the Underworld isn't for the quick. It's for the <i>dead</i>. There is no food for the quick. There is no water for the quick. The air and land itself oppresses them. The very essence of the place is dark and alien and doesn't nourish and sustain even an Exalt in the same way it does in Creation. If you're quick, and you want to go to, say, Stygia, that shouldn't be &quot;it's a long trip, pack a lunch.&quot; That should be &quot;this is a lengthy and terrifying journey through an alien realm that rejects you even as it tries to draw you in.&quot; It should be the kind of thing that even makes experienced Sijanese Funerists blanch away from you for suggesting it (that's the kind of journey they put off onto the <i>dead</i> members of their order, because trying it as one of the quick is a great way to <i>become dead</i>) and the sort of thing that even Lunars and Sidereals should react to by wanting to talk to one of the few specially trained experts in that kind of thing among their own ranks. (This is the reason dudes like Black Ice Shadow <i>exist</i>.)<br /> <br /> There are, of course, places where the realms of the quick and the dead come together. Thorns is such a place now! There are lots of little ancestor cults and shadowlands all across Creation. But the shadowlands are not the Underworld; they're actually considerably more hospitable to the quick and they're <i>still</i> pretty bad.<br /> <br /> I would really like the Underworld to not be a place you can just tool up and barge into. It isn't Creation's weird goth brother who you can go visit sometimes.<br /> <br /> And that's okay. The Underworld is for ghosts. And Abyssals. And Liminals. It doesn't also have to be for everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Sidereals who have enough brain cells to seriously consider the Underworld a major threat, realize that the Contagion was connected to it, investigate the Underworld enough to notice that something was stirring, and have <i>plans for how to help the Dragon-Blooded combat it</i>, not being completely blindsided by Thorns because &quot;Herp derp, it was outside of Fate, like, it never occured to me that anything could come from there!&quot; In 2E and especially 1E this made them look very stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>People keep saying this and I'm always baffled by it.<br /> <br /> You know who is aware the Great Contagion came out of the Underworld? The Neverborn and the Deathlords, and that's it. (<i>Maybe</i> some Abyssals.) Can you explain to me how the Sidereals are supposed to get intel out of those people? The Sidereals are pretty good at sussing out secrets, but sometimes things get past them, and &quot;a Deathlord we barely know exists hauls a doom plague we didn't know was possible out of a hole in reality we also don't know exists, located in an inaccessible part of the death world where we rarely go, and she didn't tell anyone except her Deathlord buddies&quot; seems like it should be one of those things.<br /> <br /> Prior to Thorns, why should they consider the Underworld a major threat, especially now in 3e with the Deathlords being significantly scaled back in power and reach? In the close to five thousand year history of Creation prior to Mask of Winters rolling in and being all &quot;'sup fools, Scarlet's gone and it is my time to shine now!&quot; can you name one significant threat the Underworld has actually thrown at Creation that the Sidereals would know about?<br /> <br /> Should the Sidereals have been keeping an eye on the place? Why, yes, they should... and they do! Black Ice Shadow exists because the Sidereals were like &quot;hey, keeping an eye on the Underworld is one of the things we do, and we have a chance to get ourselves a Chosen of Saturn who is deeply steeped in its essence and mysteries. Sounds good, let's do it!&quot;<br /> <br /> But there's a difference between keeping an eye on the place and devoting significant resources to it, especially given how overworked and overstretched the Sidereals are. They also keep an eye on Malfeas, but they don't invest significant resources into <i>that</i> either, because they're really very sure that the Yozi's cannot, in fact, escape. This is how the Ebon Dragon managed to run his wedding past them in 1e and 2e. The Sidereals cannot be everywhere at once.<br /> <br /> You are absolutely correct that the Sidereals should have spies and agents and webs of contacts in the Underworld. But there is a difference between that, and &quot;we know secrets even the Deathlords hold close among their damned company.&quot; The Underworld is just not going to be that important to them unless it gives them a reason to be. &quot;There are ghost-kings called Deathlords; they're pretty powerful in the context of the Underworld&quot; isn't that reason. &quot;They can roll up into Creation and fuck up a major city-state&quot; <i>is</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:38:25-07:00","id":886230,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/830716-the-underworld-peach\">I'm looking for something like this.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:36:58-07:00","id":886299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886172#post886172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain to me how the Sidereals are supposed to get intel out of those people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should they have to beg other people pretty please to tell them secrets? It's called research and investigation. They should be good at it. They can start with the fact that the Contagion was a supernatural disease that they couldn't predict, so it clearly came from outside of Fate, which means there are <i>only three</i> possible places it could come from that they could be aware of. In 760 years it never even once occurred to them that the Underworld was one of those 3 places and that it <i>might</i> be a potential threat to Creation? For 1500 years they forgot it even existed? Then they're complete idiots. Deleting the Blind Seers sidebar doesn't help if the Sidereals are still written as though it's canon.<br /> <br /> Either the Sidereals specifically are Blind Seers, or <i>everybody</i> forgot the Underworld existed.<br /> <br /> If the Underworld is so boring and monotonous and pointless that everybody in Creation and Heaven forgot it existed for all of the 5500 years after it was created, except for briefly stealing Necromancy from it, until Thorns happened, then that's a problem with the Underworld being <i>boring and monotonous and pointless</i>.<br /> <br /> There should be reasons for the living to interact with the Underworld, more than just the Deathlords. It should be and interesting place where things happen that the living can care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:55:09-07:00","id":886314,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals are aware the Great Contagion came from the Underworld. That's why the Green Lady was assigned to keep an eye on the Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:17:18-07:00","id":886326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886299#post886299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should they have to beg other people pretty please to tell them secrets? It's called research and investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Sidereals are not, in fact, mind-readers, and they don't have access to everything everywhere. They only have a limited number of resources to devote to research and investigation. They don't even have full information on everything that happens in the Realm, where they exercise broad control over its social institutions and are nominally allied with its ruler. Getting information on what the cabal of shadowy ghosts who are big wheels in the Underworld is up to is going to be way harder. Even knowing that there's vital information to be had is a heavy lift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can start with the fact that the Contagion was a supernatural disease that they couldn't predict, so it clearly came from outside of Fate, which means there are <i>only three</i> possible places it could come from that they could be aware of. </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely true. How do you prove it, and how many resources do you invest into proving it?<br /> <br /> Because &quot;well, this <i>could</i> have come from the Underworld&quot; is a great reason to devote some resources into investigating the Underworld. How many resources do you pour down that hole until you discover a lead that might or might not exist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be reasons for the living to interact with the Underworld, more than just the Deathlords. It should be and interesting place where things happen that the living can care about. </div> </div> </div>Those reasons have always existed at the liminal places where life and death intersect, and have usually centered on how the Underworld impinges on Creation, which is, of necessity, going to be Creation-centric rather than Underworld-centric. You don't usually go the other way around, and I would argue you shouldn't. The boundary between life and death shouldn't be something trivial.<br /> <br /> Narrative spaces that are heavily Underworld-centric should focus on providing an interesting playing space for 1) the dead, and 2) the dead-adjacent, the Abyssals and Liminals. Trying to shoehorn the living into them seems like a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:29:50-07:00","id":886339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886299#post886299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should they have to beg other people pretty please to tell them secrets? It's called research and investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using your skills at research and investigation, would you care to tell me what I just ate? After all, you're only half a world away (as opposed to the Sidereals, who live two worlds away), have no clues or evidence (besides my confession that I did, in fact, eat something, which again puts you a step ahead of the Sidereals), and seem to hold the position that investigators should be above having to ask people questions.<br /> <br /> Just to be fair I'll give you 760 years, though this should be a <i>much</i> simpler mystery to unravel\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:21:27-07:00","id":886393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886172#post886172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it should do that.</div> </div> </div> </div> No mote recovery was a boring disincentive mostly dependent on OOC factors and shot in the head by the fact that so few things down there had the kind of threat level to be a problem.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:25:21-07:00","id":886397,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I'm not writing clearly (<i>this is not sarcasm</i>). I don't think the Sidereals should know that the Deathlords, specifically, caused the Contagion. I think they should have enough external reasons and native intelligence to regard the Underworld as a genuine threat, pay <i><b>some</b></i> attention to it, and in time figure out that the Contagion came from there. <b><i>Long</i></b> before the Deathlords marched armies into Creation. Centuries before. They should really have paid at least some attention to it at least since the Usurpation, if not the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> I've also always believed, as a basic setting axiom, that the different realms <i><b>are</b></i> different enough from each other that their essence, creations, denizens, and materials can be distinguished from each other with some educated research and investigation: that, for example, if a savant took some Malfean brass, some quintessence metal, some mundane brass, and some grave-goods brass, and compared them, they could tell they're not identical substances and with some time and effort, figure out which is which. I assume that those substances, like the essence of the different realms, are actually <i><b>not</b></i> identical. That an informed savant can tell a Celestial gorilla god apart from a Blood Ape. That Exalts in a shadowland can tell that they've entered a different place because the essence feels different, or just doesn't come to them. (In the real world scientists can tell apart the raw materials from different locations on the same exact planet, from isotope ratios. Here we're talking about separate <b><i>universes</i></b>. I can't imagine they wouldn't differ in noticeable ways, or that all the research and knowledge of the First Age would never have uncovered any of those ways.) Until just now, it had never occured to me that (outside my headcanon?) it could be truly <b><i>impossible</i></b> to determine that the Contagion (or any other Underworld thing/phenomenon/substance) came from the Underworld. That just doesn't fit my strong mental image of the worlds being fundamentally different from one another, down to their essence.<br /> <br /> To me there are only 3 possible explanations:<br /> Sidereal blindness to everything outside of Fate until after it personally attacks them;<br /> the Underworld being so boring and empty that until the Deathlords showed themselves, <b><i>everybody</i></b> mostly just ignored it.<br /> and/or the Underworld being so impossible to interact with that nobody alive, not even millennia-old First Age Exalts, are able to learn anything about it.<br /> Whichever it is, I don't like the setting being that way.<br /> <br /> The Underworld shouldn't be boring and empty, it ought to be filled with memories of everything that's ever been important to anybody who's still a ghost and many who aren't, in the entire history of Creation since at least the last part of the Primordial War. It should be packed with stuff superimposed on/mingled with other stuff, juxtaposing different eras of history, interacting in weird ways. Things should happen. The dead should do stuff. I also think they should definitely be people, even if they can't be called human anymore due to the lack of body and po and &quot;life-force&quot; (for lack of a better word).<br /> <br /> I'd like reasons to care about the Underworld, other than &quot;OMG The World Is Coming To An End!&quot; Hopefully instead of that. I'm never likely to care as much as an Abyssals fan, but until now, other than the apparently immanent end of the world, I didn't feel a reason to care at all. It all looked so boring and empty to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:29:48-07:00","id":886402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886397#post886397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm not being clear. I don't think the Sidereals should know that the Deathlords, specifically, caused the Contagion. I think they should have enough external reasons and native intelligence to regard the Underworld as a genuine threat, pay <i><b>some</b></i> attention to it, and in time figure out that the Contagion came from there. <b><i>Long</i></b> before the Deathlords marched armies into Creation. Centuries before. They should really have paid at least some attention to it at least since the Usurpation, if not the Primordial War.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have been paying attention to the Underworld. The issue is that the Sidereal Agent, the Green Lady, is compromised. She is no longer sure were her loyalties lie anymore. <br /> <br /> One of my Sidereal Plot ideas I had is a circle of Sidereals tasked with bring the Green Lady in for questioning. Because there is NO way she didn't know about the Mask of Winters marching on Thorns. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:57:09-07:00","id":886448,"title":"","content":"Sidereals have finite resources, made even more finite by their decision to promote Dragon-Blooded rule and suppress the Solars and Lunars. By definition, any time a Sid is assigned to something, that means another assignment is no longer tasked.<br /> <br /> So, how many of the 80-ish Sids that are active at any given time should be given the job of monitoring the Underworld, the Wyld, and Malfeas (all outside of Fate) instead of taking care of Creation and Yu-Shan? I can see the conversation now...<br /> <br /> Brindle, called the Worrier, Chosen of Battles: &quot;Sifu Kejak, we need another two operatives to beef up our efforts in the Underworld. We suspect that the Contagion may have originated there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chejop Kejak, called the Poor Overworked Bastard, Chosen of Secrets: &quot;Look Brindle, we have been through this. The Fae have fallen to in-fighting, but they still occupy a good portion of Creation's borders. I've got people tied up keeping tabs on them WHILE avoiding the damned Lunars. And then of course I need to protect the infant &quot;Realm&quot; from the Lunars until they can breed their numbers back up.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, this upjumped &quot;Scarlet Empress&quot; is my only way to control the Sword of Creation, and she has the temerity to <b>demand</b> my time, and the time of our best Sifus to teach her damnable brood. I have no choice but to honor her requests, because she could die at any moment, and we need replacements for her throne. The last six hundred years demonstrated that only a single strong ruler has any chance of chaining the Dragon's Blood.<br /> <br /> The gods that survived down there are angry and resentful. They are already forming cartels to demand worship and sandbag the proper working of Creation if they don't get what they want. Most of the Censors died fighting the Crusade. Those that didn't are now tacitly supporting the hubris of &quot;Elemental Courts,&quot; to allow themselves to work less and get more power in the process. Meanwhile, dozens of gods are out of work, and a decent number of them are working for now working for Thulio. So, I need to send people to beg the Censors to their jobs, cow the gods, and hopefully head off Thulio's recruiting efforts.<br /> <br /> So, tell me, Brindle, which of those efforts would you short-change?&quot;<br /> <br /> Brindle: &quot;I apologize, Sifu. You are of course correct. I only wish to prevent another Contagion.&quot;<br /> <br /> Chejop: &quot;And the Empress is our best hope for that. As long as we have her to guard Creation and wield the Sword, everything will be fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> ===Answer to OP===<br /> <br /> The most important thing I want from the Underworld is playability.<br /> <br /> I want the Neverborn in the background, stuck in their hole, with &quot;I Suck and Die Prana&quot; running full-tilt. The tail-end of 2E became so bogged down in the &quot;doings&quot; of the Neverborn, when they really shouldn't be &quot;acting&quot; at all. They are a source of trouble, yes, but they aren't supposed to be in the spotlight.<br /> <br /> I want the Deathlords to be varied and depowered. As others have said, when the Deathlords are E10 Super-Solars, all bent on the conquest and destruction of Creation, it's hard to just tell stories and have fun.<br /> <br /> I want Abyssals to have enough narrative freedom to be playable in a standard mixed group. I also want more narratives for all-Abyssal groups than &quot;We gonna fuck Creation up, heh heh,&quot; and &quot;OMG we ran away from the Deathlords keep running!&quot;<br /> <br /> I want the Underworld itself to be an interesting, though formidable, place to explore for normal PCs. But, I also need, as a ST, to be able to push it into the background. Strange, occult planes of existence can siphon attention away from a core story pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:59:14-07:00","id":886450,"title":"","content":"Was she not sent specifically to spy on Deathlords, only in the wake of Thorns (or that other Deathlord who invaded the North earlier)? I mean paying attention in the centuries <i><b>before</b></i> that. And if she was down there before, how did nobody, including her, even know that there were Deathlords at all? (I don't mean what they were capable of, but the fact of their existence and their total conquest of Stygia.)<br /> <br /> If canonically it's truly impossible to learn, with any amount of knowledge, what world a person, thing, essence pattern, essence regeneration, magical material, or phenomenon came from, then my understanding of the entire game and absolutely everything in it is just ... incompatible with everything in the books? It would be a huge <i><b>drastic</b></i> mismatch.<br /> <br /> Edit: If the Sidereals do, in fact, regard the Underworld as so unimportant that it is not a threat to Creation, so there is no reason to devote any attention to it (until Thorns), then either they're stupid or the Underworld is cloaked in an Arcane Fate/Super Boringness/Somebody Elses' Problem Field effect that makes everybody ignore it all the time. In the latter case there's no reason for living characters to interact with it... <b><i>ever</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:03:05-07:00","id":886456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886450#post886450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was she not sent specifically to spy on Deathlords, only in the wake of Thorns (or that other Deathlord who invaded the North earlier)? I mean paying attention in the centuries <i><b>before</b></i> that. And if she was down there before, how did nobody, including her, even know that there were Deathlords at all? (I don't mean what they were capable of, but the fact of their existence and their total conquest of Stygia.)<br /> <br /> If canonically it's actually impossible to learn, with any amount of knowledge, what world a person, thing, essence pattern, essence regeneration, magical material, or phenomenon came from, then my understanding of the entire game and absolutely everything in it is just ... incompatible with everything in the books? It would be a huge <i><b>drastic</b></i> mismatch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shit. I thought she was on that assignment for centuries. Well, I'm head canoning she was assigned to the project just after the Great Contagion! One plot hole fixed! A hundred more to go! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:11:52-07:00","id":886466,"title":"","content":"My headcanon is that the Underworld is <b><i>very</i></b> interesting, and that the Exalted have regarded it as a threat and paid attention to it <i><b>continually</b></i> since the Primordial War. That Thorns took them by surprise in scale and suddenness and having an undead Behemoth and Abyssals, not that the informed high-up Exalted were totally shocked by the existence of conquering ghost-lords who had already conquered Stygia. In my headcanon the Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, and the Guild all maintain contact with ghosts and ghost-bloods who they try to use as networks of agents and spies, as well as occasionally sending actual Exalted down there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:14:45-07:00","id":886473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886466#post886466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon is that the Underworld is <b><i>very</i></b> interesting, and that the Exalted have regarded it as a threat and paid attention to it <i><b>continually</b></i> since the Primordial War. That Thorns took them by surprise in scale and suddenness and having an undead Behemoth and Abyssals, not that the informed high-up Exalted were totally shocked by the existence of conquering ghost-lords who had already conquered Stygia. In my headcanon the Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, and the Guild all maintain contact with ghosts and ghost-bloods who they try to use as networks of agents and spies, as well as occasionally sending actual Exalted down there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For every hundred plots and schemes, there is going to be ONE that was missed. That one scheme was the Mask of Winter's conquest of Thorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:37:53-07:00","id":886504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886397#post886397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I'm not writing clearly (<i>this is not sarcasm</i>). I don't think the Sidereals should know that the Deathlords, specifically, caused the Contagion. I think they should have enough external reasons and native intelligence to regard the Underworld as a genuine threat, pay <i><b>some</b></i> attention to it, and in time figure out that the Contagion came from there. <b><i>Long</i></b> before the Deathlords marched armies into Creation. Centuries before. They should really have paid at least some attention to it at least since the Usurpation, if not the Primordial War.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a hundred percent right, of course, except maybe figuring out that the Contagion came specifically from the Underworld, but... what on earth exists in the published materiel in the prior editions that gives you the impression they aren't doing that?<br /> <br /> You know who is an excellent example of them taking the Underworld seriously? Black Ice Shadow, who dates back to the 1e Sidereals core.<br /> <br /> Black Ice Shadow <i>predates</i> Thorns. His entire genesis, upbringing, and Exaltation predate the emergence of the Abyssals, or, indeed, the disappearance of the Empress and the return of the Solars. The Sidereal Exalted invested a lot of time, energy, and resources into him, and they did it specifically because keeping an eye on the Underworld and having someone who really understands it on-staff is important to them. They regard the Underworld as a genuine threat, but their evaluation of the degree of threat it represents is much lower than it <i>actually is</i>. The &quot;is a threat&quot; axis is a very long one, and until recently &quot;the Underworld&quot; was probably on it but not very high on it. <i>It should have been higher</i>. But they didn't know that! And that's both okay and believable!<br /> <br /> You know what other non-Creation realm the Sidereals are tasked with monitoring? Malfeas. There isn't a lot of wordcount devoted to that, but it exists; it is mentioned that the Sidereal Exalted occasionally find it necessary to dispatch their members to the Demon City on one task or another, and that they try and maintain intelligence networks there.<br /> <br /> Know what they completely fucking missed? The Ebon Dragon's impending nuptials and the genesis of the Infernal Exalted. Blindsided them. Because it turns out that just &quot;keeping an eye on a place&quot; isn't sufficient to let you catch everything that goes down there, especially if the powers that be that live there are trying to keep shit secret. The Sidereals don't know what they don't know.<br /> <br /> Now, you <i>could</i>, with very little effort, write the setting as &quot;the Sidereals figured out that the Deathlords are the ghosts of ancient Solars specifically empowered by the Neverborn, and one of their number unleashed the Contagion, and a number of them have very real plans to conquer creation. They figured that out centuries ago and re-deployed resources appropriately. They also know that Ebby has Scarlet and are preparing plans for that, as well.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it's also possible to write the setting the other way, where they just never found any of those details out and so never deployed resources in light of it. Neither is unbelievable or inappropriate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until just now, it had never occured to me that (outside my headcanon?) it could be truly <b><i>impossible</i></b> to determine that the Contagion (or any other Underworld thing/phenomenon/substance) came from the Underworld. That just doesn't fit my strong mental image of the worlds being fundamentally different from one another, down to their essence. </div> </div> </div>Two things.<br /> <br /> One, the Contagion was hauled out of the Well of Urdr. That place is fucked up even by Underworld standards. The normal rules may not apply.<br /> <br /> Second of all, the setting-as-written is not responsible for your headcanon. There may be events and phenomena that have their genesis outside of Creation that cannot easily have their source identified. I agree that in many cases it should be possible to figure out, but not all cases, all the time, forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Exalted have regarded it as a threat and paid attention to it <i><b>continually</b></i> since the Primordial War. That Thorns took them by surprise in scale and suddenness and having an undead Behemoth and Abyssals, not that the informed high-up Exalted were totally shocked by the existence of conquering ghost-lords who had already conquered Stygia. In my headcanon the Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, and the Guild all maintain contact with ghosts and ghost-bloods who they try to use as networks of agents and spies, as well as occasionally sending actual Exalted down there. </div> </div> </div>Is this... is this not actual canon?<br /> <br /> Because all of this seems like actual canon.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:28:57-07:00","id":886550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886504#post886504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Ice Shadow <i>predates</i> Thorns. His entire genesis, upbringing, and Exaltation predate the emergence of the Abyssals, or, indeed, the disappearance of the Empress and the return of the Solars. The Sidereal Exalted invested a lot of time, energy, and resources into him, and they did it specifically because keeping an eye on the Underworld and having someone who really understands it on-staff is important to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that is actual effort... but I have to ask how old is he? 20, or 300, or 700? <i><b>When</b></i> did the Underworld finally make it onto their list of things that matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886504#post886504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their evaluation of the degree of threat it represents is much lower than it <i>actually is</i>. The &quot;is a threat&quot; axis is a very long one, and until recently &quot;the Underworld&quot; was probably on it but not very high on it. <i>It should have been higher</i>. But they didn't know that!</div> </div> </div> </div>This, right here, is my problem. To me it isn't understandable or believable. They can't know the Deathlords' plans, but they should not consider the Underworld such a low priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886504#post886504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One, the Contagion was hauled out of the Well of Urdr. That place is fucked up even by Underworld standards. The normal rules may not apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Well part of the Underworld, or a doorway to a separate universe? I have never known which. I was mistaken in thinking the Contagion was an eruption of death essence. It being the incomprehensible exception to a usually explicable multiverse I can understand. But it did <i>definitely</i> come from outside of Fate. Why were the 3 known worlds outside of Fate still such low priorities even centuries afterwards?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886504#post886504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this... is this not actual canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to any of my limited Underworld knowledge, except for that time some First Age Solars went raiding. Hence my very first sentence on this thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=885893#post885893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read much about the 1E-2E Underworld, so I apologize in advance if I mention something that's actually already there...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having read about it is partly from my impression that it's boring and empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:02:30-07:00","id":886583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886550#post886550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that is actual effort... but I have to ask how old is he? 20, or 300, or 700? <i><b>When</b></i> did the Underworld finally make it onto their list of things that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Always? What makes you think they ever considered it a thing that didn't matter? Malfeas doesn't have a canon Sidereal exalt depicted whose whole raison d'etre is &quot;understand Hell.&quot; Does that mean that they think Malfeas doesn't matter either?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This, right here, is my problem. To me it isn't understandable or believable. They can't know the Deathlords' plans, but they should not consider the Underworld such a low priority. </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> Seriously. Why should the Underworld be higher on their priority list, pre-Thorns, than it is? You seem to be approaching this from a standpoint of &quot;they need a reason not to be paying more attention to it.&quot; I would submit that this isn't how the Sidereals work. They're over-worked and under-resourced. They need a reason <i>to do</i> something before they do it, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> <i>To the best of their knowledge</i>, the Underworld is a dangerous place that often impinges on Creation in ways that are bad for it, but is not, say, on the verge of swallowing up everything. Indeed, unless provided with a convenient shadowland or the active intercession of the living, it is often nigh-impossible for the Underworld to interact with Creation at all. Given those facts, pre-Thorns, why should they be paying more attention to it than they are?<br /> <br /> I mean... let's say, <i>hypothetically</i>, they figure out the Contagion had its genesis in the Underworld. Okay. They'd take that seriously. They'd devote extra time and attention to the place.<br /> <br /> For how many decades and centuries are they meant to continue doing that if they keep coming up with jack shit? Which they will, because in-between the Contagion and Thorns, there is, literally, nothing for them TO come up with beyond &quot;the Deathlords are very powerful and are consolidating their power as unquestioned rulers of the dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the only thing in the reports is &quot;we still have no idea where or how or who in the Underworld unleashed that thing. We suspect the Deathlords just because they're super-powerful and super-crazy, but that's mere supposition. Nothing else abnormal seems to be going on, though&quot; how long are they going to consider that time well-spent?<br /> <br /> How long do they do that before the Bureau of Destiny decides to re-purpose those resources elsewhere, because, yes, this terrible thing did come out of the Underworld, but they apparently have no way of determining how it is gonna happen again or even who caused it, and they're letting many years tick by with all these resources tied up in it while there are actual, concrete threats they <i>do</i> know about.<br /> <br /> And that's even if they know, for a very solid fact, that the Contagion was deployed into Creation from the Underworld. If they don't know that for sure, but just suspect, they probably spend a lot less time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't the Well part of the Underworld, instead of a separate universe? </div> </div> </div>It is, but it's a singular, weird construct within the Underworld. Sort of like the Sea of Mind. It's one of those setting MacGuffins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Contagion, to my understanding, was an eruption of death essence from outside of Fate. </div> </div> </div>Your understanding is wrong. The Contagion was a particularly virulent disease but it was not &quot;an eruption of death essence.&quot; Nor was it outside of Fate, in fact. Once it made it into Creation it was perfectly observable and modelable on the Loom. It was just unwise to do so, because it was so virulent that you could catch it just by watching it on said Loom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many places could death essence from outside of Fate possibly have come from? (Not counting Autochthonia) Even if it somehow wasn't death essence but something utterly incomprehensible... it came from outside of Fate. Why were the 3 known worlds outside of Fate still such low priorities even centuries afterwards? </div> </div> </div>Because priority is a relative thing! You seem to think the Sidereals should have abandoned all their other stuff and poured centuries worth of effort into monitoring these weird off-plane locations they have suspicions, but nothing concrete, about, just because of the Contagion.<br /> <br /> That's not how it works. The Sidereals have <i>day jobs</i>. A lot of their time is not their own. To the extent that they do set their own agendas, they have limited time and limited resources, and they're going to give the shaft to the places it seems wisest to the give the shaft to, based on what they know.<br /> <br /> Or, basically, what Totentanz said. Because Totentanz was absolutely right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 05-09-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:42:13-07:00","id":886612,"title":"","content":"Hm, I did not realize that the Loom of Fate was a potential vector, were the Pattern Spiders immune? Anyway, one thing I would like to see armies of warrior ghosts practicing lost martial arts styles and using lost martial arts charms. I am also interested in the evocations associated with ghost artifacts, as ghost artifacts have always been more common than standard artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:28:56-07:00","id":886635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886612#post886612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I did not realize that the Loom of Fate was a potential vector, were the Pattern Spiders immune?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. The Pattern Spiders are mechanical. It would be odd if even something like the Contagion could infect them; it would be like my car getting cancer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:45:17-07:00","id":886642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886583#post886583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think they ever considered it a thing that didn't matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>As you said, they made it a low priority. You even said, it is so low a priority it isn't even considered a part of their &quot;day job&quot; of protecting Creation. That doing anything would be a waste of resources that should be spent instead on their &quot;real&quot; job. That necessitates that it isn't considered a threat nor relevant to the safety of Creation, at all. (It also seems to contradict what you said earlier that they do consider it at least a minor threat. I find your posts quite confusing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886583#post886583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... let's say, <i>hypothetically</i>, they figure out the Contagion had its genesis in the Underworld. Okay. They'd take that seriously. They'd devote extra time and attention to the place.<br /> <br /> For how many decades and centuries are they meant to continue doing that if they keep coming up with jack shit? Which they will, because in-between the Contagion and Thorns, there is, literally, nothing for them TO come up with beyond &quot;the Deathlords are very powerful and are consolidating their power as unquestioned rulers of the dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which returns to the problem of the Underworld being so utterly boring and empty and useless that nothing ever, ever happens there, and everybody has good reason to ignore it. I want the Underworld to be an interesting place where stuff happens, where things other than Deathlords matter. Much like the Wyld shouldn't be (and will no longer be) a boring empty lava-lamp with nothing but Raksha in it.<br /> <br /> On the contrary, if they knew something in the Underworld had produced the Great Contagion, then that demonstrates immediately that the Underworld contains one of the most deadly, if not <i><b>the absolute most deadly</b></i>, threat to Creation. It was their duty to work to make sure they and the Dragon-Blooded both have the capability to oppose necromancy and ghosts, at the very least. To have plans other than assuming nothing else will go wrong. To make that a higher priority than faction politics. Because protecting Creation from <b><i>is</i></b> their job. If the Underworld is a threat to Creation, paying attention to it <b><i>is</i></b> their job, not an irrelevant distraction and waste of resources.<br /> <br /> If they somehow learned that the Contagion came specifically from the Well of Urd and is (according to forumites) impossible to ever replicate no matter what, then it no longer makes sense to consider the Underworld the greatest threat to Creation. Not until Thorns, at least. But how the heck would they know that? Even then, it would still be foolish to downgrade it to a trivial threat or none at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886583#post886583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor was it outside of Fate, in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I thought the entire Underworld is outside of Fate. (<i>Not being sarcastic.</i>) I know there's a Calendar of Setesh there instead of a Loom of Fate. I don't have either Sidereal book, but everybody on the entire internet has always, always called the Underworld outside of Fate, and I always believed the unanimous consensus. Until after the Contagion had already started killing people, it was not in Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886583#post886583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to think the Sidereals should have abandoned all their other stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that isn't what I meant. I think they should not put it on the <i><b>lowest</b></i> priority or ignore it completely in favor of things that are not in any way a threat to Creation, like heretics against the Immaculate dogma.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However, this tangent is not useful to this thread. You and I are never going to agree about any subject whatsoever related to Sidereal fallibility. I think they made mistakes and should be depicted as more involved in the Underworld. You disagree. Enough.<br /> <br /> To return to the OP, I think the Underworld should be an interesting place where lots of <i><b>non</b></i>-Deathlord stuff is happening. Not somewhere boring and empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:31:12-07:00","id":886676,"title":"","content":"Erinys, if you refuse to accept that a choice <i>that turns out only in hindsight to be bad</i> can be made for reasons other than pants-on-head stupidity, well, there really <i>is</i> nowhere this conversation can go.<br /> <br /> Also, the Underworld not teeming with threats on par with the Great Contagion <b>does not</b> mean an empty Underworld. Just an Underworld that the Sidereals might underestimate. You know, as people do.<br /> <br /> So what <i>did</i> I eat earlier? Didja figure that out yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:01:03-07:00","id":886702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886172#post886172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it should do that.<br /> <br /> The Underworld should not, in my opinion, be a place you can just walk into for a day trip. Even if they aren't going to go the full &quot;the fact that the Underworld exists at all is a fucked-up mistake created by the Exalted murdering things that shouldn't have been capable of being murdered&quot; on it, it shouldn't be the kind of place that the quick, even the Exalted, can easily penetrate deep into.<br /> <br /> Because the Underworld isn't for the quick. It's for the <i>dead</i>. There is no food for the quick. There is no water for the quick. The air and land itself oppresses them. The very essence of the place is dark and alien and doesn't nourish and sustain even an Exalt in the same way it does in Creation. If you're quick, and you want to go to, say, Stygia, that shouldn't be &quot;it's a long trip, pack a lunch.&quot; That should be &quot;this is a lengthy and terrifying journey through an alien realm that rejects you even as it tries to draw you in.&quot; It should be the kind of thing that even makes experienced Sijanese Funerists blanch away from you for suggesting it (that's the kind of journey they put off onto the <i>dead</i> members of their order, because trying it as one of the quick is a great way to <i>become dead</i>) and the sort of thing that even Lunars and Sidereals should react to by wanting to talk to one of the few specially trained experts in that kind of thing among their own ranks. (This is the reason dudes like Black Ice Shadow <i>exist</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This presentation isn't without its virtues, but it's wholly incompatible with making the underworld a place where I could run a campaign of any given Exalted, so it definitely has to be one or the other. For my money, making the danger of the underworld &quot;you can't get the basic necessities of life or the things you need to power all the game's mechanics&quot; is probably the least interesting way to go about it. You can, in fact, make the Underworld a deeply creepy, dangerous and unpleasant place for the living without making it a bad place to set a Lunars game, but it means prioritizing playability above aesthetic statements, as is done with all the other best-designed parts of the setting. Doing it that way also has the upside that you don't need to give Abyssals, who are alive, pages of baseline exceptions just to let them play in the location designed especially for them.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: if you want the underworld to be so deleterious that it's a harrowing journey even for a circle of Celestial Exalted to visit, then it's absurd for the underworld to be a <i>world</i> at all, because the game is entirely about the living. at that point you might as well have the entire Underworld just be the labyrinth and shadowlands. And, in fact, that's pretty close to what we got in previous editions, except that for every such place they felt obligated to add a thousand miles squared of bland Ghost Prairies full of plasmic animals (which are like regular animals, but spooky) and green peasants who have spent 1000 years of undeath pretending to farm turnips. The scale and potential of the underworld, when contrasted with its unusability as a campaign setting, is absurd, and sure enough, nobody uses the underworld as a campaign setting.<br /> <br /> I bet the Malfean acid-sea Kimbery is full of ancient sunken cities and weird demonic races and stuff, and you can't ever go there because it's a sea made of acid, and if you did it would indeed be a harrowing &quot;get in, get out&quot; journey racing against the clock. But the game doesn't waste any space talking about that, because that's not a setting, it's <i>at best </i>an 0D&amp;D dungeon crawl. We already have the Labyrinth for that; dedicating the whole underworld to the same purpose would be wasting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 05-09-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:09:03-07:00","id":886711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886550#post886550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that is actual effort... but I have to ask how old is he? 20, or 300, or 700? <i><b>When</b></i> did the Underworld finally make it onto their list of things that matter?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>However old he is, he might also have had a predecessor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:24:44-07:00","id":886775,"title":"","content":"I think that the main reason why the Underworld should be dangerous would be the ghosts that exist within its borders. Every ghost is an essence user and there are potentially a lot more ghosts than there are people in Creation (if 5% of the people since the Usurpation are still ghosts in the Underworld, the number of ghosts in Creation would be tenfold the number of people in Creation). While the vast majority of them probably do not have the initiative or the desire to be a practitioner of supernatural martial arts, even if 0.01% of ghosts are practitioners of supernatural martial arts, that would mean that there would be around 400,000 ghostly practitioners of the supernatural martial arts. In addition, the remainder of the ghosts could be dangerous in their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:46:09-07:00","id":886838,"title":"","content":"Once again, Aya Tari, the number of presumptions made by you is baffling and makes the object of a post ludicrous all the way to the foundation.<br /> <br /> Why assume that one in twenty ghosts <i>from over a thousand years ago</i> have persisted to this day? Why assume that there are more ghosts in the Underworld than there are people in Creation, if not to arrive at your ridiculous premise?<br /> <br /> For that matter, why assume that they can even practice supernatural martial arts like Exalts? Oh, wait, I already know the answer: because they could in 2e and in spite of dev and author commentary suggesting otherwise, you're going to keep it that way because it isn't <i>explicitly</i> in a book yet. Am I close to the mark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:27:02-07:00","id":886875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886136#post886136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s some fairly fundamental baggage attached to the idea of if ghosts should exist or if they\u2019re even really people anymore coupled with a tendency to have undead kingdoms that could work just as easily or better as living ones.<br /> <br /> For example, the dual kingdom of Hanau and Tyoka is pretty cool because its throne is shared by Princess Annuaski and her ancestor Queen Defiance-in-Shadow two monarchs from different points in history with very different styles of rule.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this dual ruler dynamic is expressed as a Summer/Winter Court where Annuaski frequently wastes all the resources leaving Defiance-in-Shadow's half of the year to be a time of austerity and hardship that sucks and if these were two spirits ruling over a mortal population most of my characters would be all over deposing Annuaski yesterday but... when you give it a moments thought, food, warmth and shelter are strictly comfort things for a ghost and if half a year of excess lets them forget that they're stuck in limbo I'm not going to judge, <i>however</i> I don't think we were supposed to look at it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with a lot of the points both you and the others here have made, I still don't understand why people don't just change things to fit their needs. Is it ideal? No, not even close. However, the Exalted community has a long history of the players homebrewing and doing things to change the game so that they can enjoy it the way they want. I do want to say, as a closing remark, that I feel the UW suffered greatly from a large portion of it being an undefined grey space (a lot more so than many of the 2e bland areas in Creation). After all, each direction got its own setting book, which helped immenesly when fleshing out areas for people to campaign in. However, the UW only got one book...that just meant it was a hell of a lot more work if you were a ST and wanted to game in a place not mentioned in the setting splat for the UW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:35:41-07:00","id":886880,"title":"","content":"What I want from the underworld;<br /> <br /> Basically what I already have. <br /> Floating islands awash upon a tumultuous ocean. Each island an 'afterlife' for a person or community or souls with common interests. <br /> Each island under the threat that maybe, today is the day the iron-wrought horror of the hundred island compact under the sway of The Deathlord swings by and gobbles you up for all eternity. <br /> Each island inhabitant caught between tossing themselves into the churning ocean and accepting their final end and reincarnation or holding on to whatever scrap of purpose they have left. <br /> <br /> What I don't want from the underworld is;<br /> Life-but-not. I want death to be DEATH and not just a gateway into another world exactly the same but with different bastards trying to enslave you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:40:44-07:00","id":886888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886702#post886702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This presentation isn't without its virtues, but it's wholly incompatible with making the underworld a place where I could run a campaign of any given Exalted, so it definitely has to be one or the other. For my money, making the danger of the underworld &quot;you can't get the basic necessities of life or the things you need to power all the game's mechanics&quot; is probably the least interesting way to go about it. You can, in fact, make the Underworld a deeply creepy, dangerous and unpleasant place for the living without making it a bad place to set a Lunars game, but it means prioritizing playability above aesthetic statements, as is done with all the other best-designed parts of the setting. Doing it that way also has the upside that you don't need to give Abyssals, who are alive, pages of baseline exceptions just to let them play in the location designed especially for them.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: if you want the underworld to be so deleterious that it's a harrowing journey even for a circle of Celestial Exalted to visit, then it's absurd for the underworld to be a <i>world</i> at all, because the game is entirely about the living. at that point you might as well have the entire Underworld just be the labyrinth and shadowlands. And, in fact, that's pretty close to what we got in previous editions, except that for every such place they felt obligated to add a thousand miles squared of bland Ghost Prairies full of plasmic animals (which are like regular animals, but spooky) and green peasants who have spent 1000 years of undeath pretending to farm turnips. The scale and potential of the underworld, when contrasted with its unusability as a campaign setting, is absurd, and sure enough, nobody uses the underworld as a campaign setting.<br /> <br /> I bet the Malfean acid-sea Kimbery is full of ancient sunken cities and weird demonic races and stuff, and you can't ever go there because it's a sea made of acid, and if you did it would indeed be a harrowing &quot;get in, get out&quot; journey racing against the clock. But the game doesn't waste any space talking about that, because that's not a setting, it's <i>at best </i>an 0D&amp;D dungeon crawl. We already have the Labyrinth for that; dedicating the whole underworld to the same purpose would be wasting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gayo, while I do agree with your sentiments here, I'd ask a follow on question and this is &quot;How would you do what you've described?&quot; How would you implement and change the UW so that it is still the spooky/horrific place we all want it to be, but for it to still mesh with the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T20:05:29-07:00","id":886910,"title":"","content":"Kimbery is actually a setting and, with the right Infernal charms, PCs can survive a visit to her.<br /> <br /> But the rest of Hell is infinite and some other Yozis are easier for non-Infernals to visit.<br /> <br /> (Not trying to make any point in this post, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2016, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T22:20:50-07:00","id":886981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886888#post886888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gayo, while I do agree with your sentiments here, I'd ask a follow on question and this is &quot;How would you do what you've described?&quot; How would you implement and change the UW so that it is still the spooky/horrific place we all want it to be, but for it to still mesh with the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he included some suggestions there - food that doesn't nourish, water that doesn't sate. Sleepless nights. Things that see the blood of the living as the sweetest of wines. Throw in the complex politics generated by cramming a hundred years of dead people into the same physical space, blend it with the insanity produced by them all trying to find meaning after Creation has largely passed you by, and let it loose right next door to a nation slain a thousand years ago by the Great Contagion, and you have a place where short trips are dangerous and long trips are foolhardy.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there'd still be ways to venture in there for the living and especially for the Abyssal and Liminal Exalted. A well-equipped caravan might venture through a shadowland into a deeper kingdom and return with graveborn ivory harvested from plasmic mastodons. A Solar might use his incredible mastery of survival to literally find food where none should exist. A Lunar might just say &quot;Who needs food when you can be a camel?&quot;<br /> <br /> Challenges great enough to deter mortals don't need to be harsh enough that the Exalted consider it a no-go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T23:10:09-07:00","id":887006,"title":"","content":"And the fact that it's a spirit realm means the &quot;laws&quot; of the Underworld don't have to be the same as Creation. Hell, they don't even have to be the same from one area to another. There might be taboos that aren't just social but help feed into keeping the world stable. Taboos that are daily ritual of some kind, not unlike a constant prayer that holds their land together. You can do a lot of very interesting things with that. It could create dangers that aren't some beast, a lack of resources, or harsh environment. And if you are ignoring it, you are endangering lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T00:08:26-07:00","id":887027,"title":"","content":"I really don't care much for Exalted Underworld, too European for Jen with all its lord and knight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T00:25:47-07:00","id":887032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887027#post887027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't care much for Exalted Underworld, too European for Jen with all its lord and knight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they have a place there, BUT... they shouldn't be the only thing by far, and that's a problem. It's part of the reason I think it's fallen flat before and you hit it right on the nose. What there is lacks... variety of many kinds. And all the lord/knight stuff was baked in there right from the beginning. While the problems were different, I've started to feel like Abyssals and the Underworld were as flawed as Lunars, straight from their first focus books. So thanks for pointing that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T01:16:53-07:00","id":887042,"title":"","content":"Can someone provide me with a link to the official discussion concerning ghosts not being able to practice martial arts since I seemed to have missed something? I would not be surprised, per se, just disappointed that they got rid of another aspect of 1e that I liked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T05:27:34-07:00","id":887091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887042#post887042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone provide me with a link to the official discussion concerning ghosts not being able to practice martial arts since I seemed to have missed something?</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't, I was just making a point. But, that said, the core book section on martial arts in fact specifies that this is what happens when <i>Exalted</i> practice martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:38:00-07:00","id":887148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886875#post886875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with a lot of the points both you and the others here have made, I still don't understand why people don't just change things to fit their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. What you're overlooking in that statement is that we're discussing what's wrong with the canonical Underworld because canon is like true north on a compass.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:49:43-07:00","id":887156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886775#post886775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every ghost is an essence user and there are potentially a lot more ghosts than there are people in Creation (if 5% of the people since the Usurpation are still ghosts in the Underworld, the number of ghosts in Creation would be tenfold the number of people in Creation). While the vast majority of them probably do not have the initiative or the desire to be a practitioner of supernatural martial arts, even if 0.01% of ghosts are practitioners of supernatural martial arts, that would mean that there would be around 400,000 ghostly practitioners of the supernatural martial arts. In addition, the remainder of the ghosts could be dangerous in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume, and would find the setting to be consistent with the idea, that the majority of spirits of all types only have fairly minor and personally useful powers.<br /> <br /> I do this because I find priorities that amount to &quot;make enormous workforces of spirits&quot; to kind of focus games away from human interests.<br /> <br /> The idea of somebody having an army of ghosts at their beck and call has its values, but I think it should be distinctly ghostly; something you could direct to haunt and blight and possess. Reducing it down to &quot;they can use Essence, so teach them martial arts and have them make Artifacts&quot; is rather flavourless.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:50:36-07:00","id":887158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886875#post886875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with a lot of the points both you and the others here have made, I still don't understand why people don't just change things to fit their needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST, I alter the setting from Canon all the time. Yet, players will make assumptions and develop characters based on what they read. For example, if canon reads that bound demons are unlikely to backstab you and the ST wants to play up demons being the old enemies of the Exalts, there is going to be dissolution between the ST and the a demon binding player. <br /> <br /> In my last Exalted game, the ST also altered Canon a lot. We, the players, would always ask &quot;What does my character know about this?&quot; to see what our characters know about the setting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:04:10-07:00","id":887170,"title":"","content":"Yes, the majority of ghosts have minor powers, that is why I said 0.01% being practitioners of supernatural martial arts, which is about as common as making $10 million per year in the USA. I think we can all agree that people that make that much money are rare, so ghosts practitioners of the supernatural martial arts are rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:14:07-07:00","id":887178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887148#post887148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do. What you're overlooking in that statement is that we're discussing what's wrong with the canonical Underworld because canon is like true north on a compass.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. Canon is the original position from which all games begin. Even a ST with zero regard for canon is likely to retain significant portions of it simply out of time constraints. That's why we pay money for fluff; most of us don't have the time or inclination to write our own setting.<br /> <br /> So it's always valid to discuss in what ways the canon setting helps or hurts telling the stories people want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:21:06-07:00","id":887184,"title":"","content":"Rarity doesn't matter as much when you go and lump them all together to make them less special like that. <br /> <br /> Another thing to keep in mind is that the Underworld isn't written as having a population ten times higher than Creation - and with its &quot;mirror of Creation's terrain, but death-y&quot; being broken in Ex3, it would be <i>absurdly</i> dense if one in twenty people who died since the Usurpation was still around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:43:19-07:00","id":887210,"title":"","content":"Only as dense as the Shogunate Era. The Underworld of the Threshold has been described as very densely populated in previous editions, especially the Underworld of the Scavenger Lands. The victims of the Great Contagion became ghosts in large proportions because of a lack of proper funeral services to send them on to Lethe, and a large number of them still exist, the huddled masses of the Underworld that lack anyone to remember their existence. While a decent number of them have been soulforged, I do not think that there are billions of ghosts worth of soulsteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:05:31-07:00","id":887264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887210#post887210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld of the Threshold has been described as very densely populated in previous editions</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm gonna stop you there. Notwithstanding the questionable utility of citing previous Editions for other parts of the setting, the Underworld specifically is wholly different now. Assuming that anything from the 1E or 2E canon still holds true when it comes to this is frankly a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887210#post887210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a decent number of them have been soulforged, I do not think that there are billions of ghosts worth of soulsteel.</div> </div> </div> </div>...You <i>do </i>realize that there are ghostly fates other than &quot;be soulforged&quot; or &quot;persist forever&quot; right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:13:10-07:00","id":887270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887210#post887210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only as dense as the Shogunate Era. The Underworld of the Threshold has been described as very densely populated in previous editions, especially the Underworld of the Scavenger Lands. The victims of the Great Contagion became ghosts in large proportions because of a lack of proper funeral services to send them on to Lethe, and a large number of them still exist, the huddled masses of the Underworld that lack anyone to remember their existence. While a decent number of them have been soulforged, I do not think that there are billions of ghosts worth of soulsteel.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have this habit of assuming that anything true in the previous editions is true now. It's a bad habit. Ex3 has quite deliberately left behind that material to build a new setting that better reflects the needs of people telling stories. This change is revolutionary compared to the 1st to 2nd edition jump.<br /> <br /> As an example of this, the entire model of the Underworld has been tossed out and rewritten in the new core. That model shoots the notion of &quot;Underworld of the Scavenger Lands&quot; right in the head.<br /> <br /> You're much better off reading the new material, and the devs' statements regarding the intended direction, and then pondering what about the old material worked, and what did not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:32:14-07:00","id":887285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887270#post887270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're much better off reading the new material, and the devs' statements regarding the intended direction, and then pondering what about the old material worked, and what did not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not trying to extrapolate hard numbers out of mechanics meant to facilitate a cool story, for the sake of projecting onto Creation in a way that turns the new material into an absurd cartoon.<br /> <br /> But this <i>is</i> Aya &quot;10% of mortals should be sorcerers&quot; Tari we're talking about, here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:23:33-07:00","id":887387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886676#post886676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erinys, if you refuse to accept that a choice <i>that turns out only in hindsight to be bad</i> can be made for reasons other than pants-on-head stupidity, well, there really <i>is</i> nowhere this conversation can go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also too, Erinys: you've got Murc and Alucard on the same side of an argument about <i>the Underworld</i>. At that point you gotta ask yourself, &quot;How far from the pack <i>have</i> I strayed?&quot;<br /> <br /> (I kid because I love.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:08:23-07:00","id":887831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887158#post887158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an ST, I alter the setting from Canon all the time. Yet, players will make assumptions and develop characters based on what they read. For example, if canon reads that bound demons are unlikely to backstab you and the ST wants to play up demons being the old enemies of the Exalts, there is going to be dissolution between the ST and the a demon binding player.<br /> <br /> In my last Exalted game, the ST also altered Canon a lot. We, the players, would always ask &quot;What does my character know about this?&quot; to see what our characters know about the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems like an issue that the ST and players need to work out together, which should be apparent if you are going to change things about a setting or homebrew. I'm surprised there was something to read about that was canon, in a homebrew only piece of the UW. As always, its up the ST to ensure that they manage expectations and try to create a good gaming atmosphere. If players are going to use meta knowledge, instead of utilizing their character to find out things they know in the game, they've already gone down a bad road. While they can talk about how cool this demon is or how he behaves as written in this splat and what not, their character may know nothing of it in the game. Isn't that part of learning and feeling out the world the ST creates? I can only speak for myself, but I def. wouldn't want a player to start a game and then just say, I'm not making any rolls on these checks, because I already know how this thing acts, etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:15:39-07:00","id":887838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887148#post887148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're overlooking in that statement is that we're discussing what's wrong with the canonical Underworld because canon is like true north on a compass.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't agree. In fact my first post was asking Gayo what exactly what is wrong with it, in his opinion. Even more importantly, I've asked how it would be fixed (read: solutions). Anyone can bitch about something all day long (not a sleight towards Gayo or anyone else, just saying in general). Coming up with a solution to fix it, is often times much, much harder. So, I'll state again, <i><b>that I agree that much needs to be changed/fixed</b></i>, but I wonder how one would go about getting it done to the extent that it would make the majority of the players happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:22:45-07:00","id":887846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=886981#post886981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he included some suggestions there - food that doesn't nourish, water that doesn't sate. Sleepless nights. Things that see the blood of the living as the sweetest of wines. Throw in the complex politics generated by cramming a hundred years of dead people into the same physical space, blend it with the insanity produced by them all trying to find meaning after Creation has largely passed you by, and let it loose right next door to a nation slain a thousand years ago by the Great Contagion, and you have a place where short trips are dangerous and long trips are foolhardy.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there'd still be ways to venture in there for the living and especially for the Abyssal and Liminal Exalted. A well-equipped caravan might venture through a shadowland into a deeper kingdom and return with graveborn ivory harvested from plasmic mastodons. A Solar might use his incredible mastery of survival to literally find food where none should exist. A Lunar might just say &quot;Who needs food when you can be a camel?&quot;<br /> <br /> Challenges great enough to deter mortals don't need to be harsh enough that the Exalted consider it a no-go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some great ideas. But what about all the other pieces of the UW. What he described (which I missed in reading through the replies), sounds great for a (relatively) small portion of the UW. I'm specifically speaking of the nation portion, here. What about the other nations? Other lands? That ideas seems to only cover a very specific spot and it might not even cover that much when you plot it out on a map. Hopefully that makes sense.<br /> <br /> On a slightly different note, do you know if the intent is to keep the UW a mirror of Creation (i.e. its shaped the same in terms of continents/land mass, but the lands themselves are different)? If they didn't have to merry up with the sunny side of Creation, you could drastically change the medium of this UW makeover.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:00:01-07:00","id":887883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887178#post887178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Canon is the original position from which all games begin. Even a ST with zero regard for canon is likely to retain significant portions of it simply out of time constraints. That's why we pay money for fluff; most of us don't have the time or inclination to write our own setting.<br /> <br /> So it's always valid to discuss in what ways the canon setting helps or hurts telling the stories people want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't disagree with the statement and I understand that it is quite laborious to come up with tons of fluff for your own setting. I even mentioned that I wanted &quot;direction&quot; books for parts of the UW because it was the same size [as Creation], but only got 1/8 of the coverage that Creation got. It seems like there a few of you who don't understand that I'm not trying to smother and snuff out other's voices. There's nothing wrong with stating what you said, or stating that other things in the UW that didn't work...but I do think that there have been not nearly enough solutions put forth to fix the problems (and there are many). I mean, are we going compile these together, send them to the devs for use? Or is it just idle talk between us exalted players speaking of things that we hope for and no more? I'd love to see some of the ideas that have been suggested, to actually be used.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T23:29:50-07:00","id":887934,"title":"","content":"Does anyone feel that the Underworld can be interesting if its inhabitants aren't real people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T00:14:14-07:00","id":887956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887934#post887934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone feel that the Underworld can be interesting if its inhabitants aren't real people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the Crystal Gems &quot;real people?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ghosts may differ from us, but writing that dismisses their humanity outright is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T00:34:46-07:00","id":887961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887934#post887934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone feel that the Underworld can be interesting if its inhabitants aren't real people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But you need to know to what extent that's the case when you're going in because otherwise you have a famine in the kingdom of Tyoka that you're clearly supposed to care about, but when you stop and think about it its as real as an actor shuffling around stage pretending to die of thirst in the desert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:00:54-07:00","id":888094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887883#post887883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't disagree with the statement and I understand that it is quite laborious to come up with tons of fluff for your own setting. I even mentioned that I wanted &quot;direction&quot; books for parts of the UW because it was the same size [as Creation], but only got 1/8 of the coverage that Creation got. It seems like there a few of you who don't understand that I'm not trying to smother and snuff out other's voices. There's nothing wrong with stating what you said, or stating that other things in the UW that didn't work...but I do think that there have been not nearly enough solutions put forth to fix the problems (and there are many). I mean, are we going compile these together, send them to the devs for use? Or is it just idle talk between us exalted players speaking of things that we hope for and no more? I'd love to see some of the ideas that have been suggested, to actually be used.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This forum does not always provide solutions for perceived problems in the text. Sometimes we just worry it like a dog with a bone for a few days/months/Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:07:14-07:00","id":888098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887956#post887956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts may differ from us, but writing that dismisses their humanity outright is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>... how so?<br /> <br /> It would be perfectly okay to write ghosts as either more or less inhuman. Indeed, that's kind of what the point of things like Hungry Ghosts and to a lesser extent Spectres are, is it not?<br /> <br /> That said, it would also be okay to write them as extremely human indeed. Or as existing on a spectrum.<br /> <br /> But I personally have always been real uncomfortable with &quot;the dead are just like the living.&quot; They shouldn't be. They're dead. That's a hell of a state change and it should carry more weight than &quot;now I live in the Underworld and have ghost powers.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:39:09-07:00","id":888123,"title":"","content":"Hungry ghosts <i>are</i> ghosts, I suppose, but I was referring to the <i>non</i>-hungry sort, which, y'know, are typically just referred to categorically as &quot;ghosts.&quot; <br /> <br /> As for specters, they're ghosts like the object of worship in your ancestor-cult, just not the picture of mental health, given the Whispers have riddled them with mental illnesses and delusions. <br /> <br /> Really, calling either of those &quot;not human&quot; is, well, straying into pretty uncomfortable territory. You seem like a decent sort, and I don't want to accuse you of anything awful, but real-life people use some pretty similar justifications to mistreat the mentally-disabled and mentally-ill.<br /> <br /> Ghosts don't have to be exactly like the living - I didn't say they did! They lack something, that's true. But that doesn't mean you can deny their humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-11-2016, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:52:48-07:00","id":888137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888123#post888123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have to be exactly like the living - I didn't say they did! They lack something, that's true. But that doesn't mean you can deny their humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hold on now. You said specifically that <i>writing</i> ghosts as less-than-human would be straight-up wrong. That's different from what you're talking about now. If Vance (to pick a writer at random) were to write up a weird underworld kingdom where the ghosts are specifically inhuman and fucked up because reasons, I would say that would be totally okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:00:24-07:00","id":888143,"title":"","content":"Sorry, let me rephrase. <br /> <br /> <b>Writing that explicates ghosts (that is to say, the persisting souls of deceased humans) as <i>categorically</i> inhuman is bad for the game by dint of poisoning players' perceptions of them, as well as smacking of real-world prejudices against the mentally-ill and the mentally-disabled.</b><br /> <br /> Also, generally, being &quot;fucked-up&quot; doesn't stop you being human either. I feel I shouldn't have to say that but it seems I must anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:01:29-07:00","id":888144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888137#post888137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, hold on now. You said specifically that <i>writing</i> ghosts as less-than-human would be straight-up wrong. That's different from what you're talking about now. If Vance (to pick a writer at random) were to write up a weird underworld kingdom where the ghosts are specifically inhuman and fucked up because reasons, I would say that would be totally okay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just as long as there are &quot;reasons&quot;. I hate when people do inhuman and/or crazy as &quot;I do crazy shit just because.&quot; Everyone has reasons, even the mad. Their reasons may be insane, but there is a logic behind it. <br /> <br /> Even Deadpool, who talks to his audience and does some wacky random shit, has reasons for what he does. <br /> <br /> /tangant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:08:03-07:00","id":888153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888143#post888143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, let me rephrase.<br /> <br /> <b>Writing that explicates ghosts (that is to say, the persisting souls of deceased humans) as <i>categorically</i> inhuman is bad for the game by dint of poisoning players' perceptions of them, as well as smacking of real-world prejudices against the mentally-ill and the mentally-disabled.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>... why?<br /> <br /> What would be wrong with &quot;we want these entities to be fundamentally and categorically inhuman, so we're going to write them as fundamentally inhuman?&quot; I'm unclear on why morality demands that the fictional souls of fictional deceased humans in a fictional underworld <i>need</i> to retain their humanity. There's nothing wrong with writing them that way, of course, but I don't see why writing them another way is problematic at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:21:31-07:00","id":888160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888153#post888153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we're supposed to be able to do more with ghosts than Smite Evil and move on to the next 10'x10' room. We're supposed to be able to relate to them, help them, worship them, romance them, and maybe even play as them. Really hard to do these things when the books plant a flag saying, &quot;These guys aren't people, and if your character cares about them, she's deluded.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:32:11-07:00","id":888173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888160#post888160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we're supposed to be able to do more with ghosts than Smite Evil and move on to the next 10'x10' room. We're supposed to be able to relate to them, help them, worship them, romance them, and maybe even play as them. Really hard to do these things when the books plant a flag saying, &quot;These guys aren't people, and if your character cares about them, she's deluded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm confused again. Are you saying that it would be wrong to write ghosts as not being <i>people</i>, or as being <i>inhuman</i>?<br /> <br /> Demons and raksha are categorically and fundamentally inhuman. So are many spirits and gods. We can do all those things in your list with them, up to and including playing as them. High-Clarity Alchemicals, they're also pretty inhuman. But all those things are still people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:35:28-07:00","id":888180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888160#post888160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we're supposed to be able to do more with ghosts than Smite Evil and move on to the next 10'x10' room. We're supposed to be able to relate to them, help them, worship them, romance them, and maybe even play as them. Really hard to do these things when the books plant a flag saying, &quot;These guys aren't people, and if your character cares about them, she's deluded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? Why not have it both ways?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind the book defining whether ghosts are actually the spirit of your dead sister or just an echo. You can have character who want to help ghosts and characters who think you are deluded for thinking ghosts are &quot;real people&quot;. No one in Creation knows which is right, why not OOC too? Leave it up to the ST to decide which side is right if they need to decide at all. <br /> <br /> Hell, that may even work with Abyssals. Some Abyssals see ghosts as people and help them. Others see them as tools to fulfill their goals and desires. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:43:59-07:00","id":888191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888160#post888160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we're supposed to be able to do more with ghosts than Smite Evil and move on to the next 10'x10' room. We're supposed to be able to relate to them, help them, worship them, romance them, and maybe even play as them. Really hard to do these things when the books plant a flag saying, &quot;These guys aren't people, and if your character cares about them, she's deluded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing that stops players (and PCs) from caring about fundamentally inhuman beings. Since you soft-cited DnD, I'll note the internet is riddled with stories of DnD games where people take pity on supposedly evil creatures and adopt them. Hell, you and I both have seen people express pity and compassion for Demons on these forums, even the ones that are inherently inimical to human life.<br /> <br /> The game can send a message that Ghosts aren't human without denying their sapience, their capacity to feel pain, and their aspirations.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of telling meaningful stories in Exalted, I would argue that it's more important for the setting to state that Ghosts aren't human anymore, because it's that loss of humanity that gives death meaning. If you set up Ghosts to simply be people, then death isn't a consequence, or even remarkable. At worst, it becomes a power-up.<br /> <br /> I'm not willing to invalidate the consequential and compelling narratives of death in order to support some flimsy notion that dehumanization of fantasy ghosts is somehow disrespectful to people in the real-world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:34:04-07:00","id":888286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=887956#post887956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Crystal Gems &quot;real people?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ghosts may differ from us, but writing that dismisses their humanity outright is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Crystal Gems and other members of the <i>Steven Universe</i> Gem species were never human in the first place.<br /> <br /> The better analogy is to ask whether or not the fragments of shattered Gems (including the ones Clustered together) are still real people, or just corpses twitching about reflexively, without real consciousness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ghosts were once human, but they lost something essential to being human when they died. They didn't just exchange a perishable, fleshy body and a natural place in Creation for an imperishable, plasmic body and a natural place in the Underworld, plus the ability to learn ghost Charms. They LOST something.<br /> <br /> The issue is, how much did they lose, and what does that leave them? I'm not sure <i>Exalted </i>has been clear or consistent on the matter.<br /> <br /> In the <i>Dresden Files</i>, ghosts are explicitly NOT people at all, just the echoes of people. At one point, someone deliberately creates a ghost of themself through a near-death experience in order to double-team an enemy, and though the ghost acts just like the original, it's just an echo that quickly fades without being morned.<br /> <br /> What are ghosts supposed to be in <i>Exalted?</i> Do they retain enough humanity to be considered people?<br /> <br /> <br /> I asked this question back on the first page, but no one really answered. It's only after I narrowed the question down into something more challenging that you bothered to respond.<br /> <br /> I personally don't think that the Underworld can be worth much as a setting unless ghosts are somehow people.<br /> <br /> If they're just echoes without real pain and fear, then they're just moving scenery, game for hunting sports, cheap slave labor, and raw material for soulsteel. And we JUST got away from &quot;all demons are raw material for Infernal Artifacts&quot; and the damage that did to the ability to view demons as people.<br /> <br /> But how are ghosts still like people? Are they, as you suggest, best modeled as senile and mentally-disabled?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:40:01-07:00","id":888292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888286#post888286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how are ghosts still like people? Are they, as you suggest, best modeled as senile and mentally-disabled?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My head canon? Ghosts lost the ability to adapt to new situations. A ghost can not learn and grow from their post death experiences...<br /> <br /> ..unless they are mad enough to brave the Labyrinth and become Deathlords/Nephwraks. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:40:27-07:00","id":888294,"title":"","content":"I want abyssals to be world slaying apocalypse weapons loyal to Oblivion, none of this romance of the grave or deathly honor or ghost king nonsense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:57:49-07:00","id":888311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalad2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888294#post888294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want abyssals to be world slaying apocalypse weapons loyal to Oblivion, none of this romance of the grave or deathly honor or ghost king nonsense</div> </div> </div> </div>And I want the very opposite. Abyssals as nothing more than Oblivion's sociopathic world-killers lack depth, interest, playability, and a host of other positive aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:58:54-07:00","id":888315,"title":"","content":"Since I hate the suggestion that Infernals should be inherently evil with no moral agency or free will, I also want Abyssals to have moral agency, and the power to tell the Neverborn and Deathlords to suck it and become antiheroes. Let people tell that story about Abyssals if they want it. It isn't going to make evil loyalist Abyssals disappear if others go renegade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:21:35-07:00","id":888332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888311#post888311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I want the very opposite. Abyssals as nothing more than Oblivion's sociopathic world-killers lack depth, interest, playability, and a host of other positive aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't find &quot;end the world&quot; to be an interesting campaign goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:27:36-07:00","id":888339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalad2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888332#post888332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't find &amp;quot;end the world&amp;quot; to be an interesting campaign goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is only so many times you can end the world before the Apocalypse grows dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:17:25-07:00","id":888382,"title":"","content":"At least according to previous editions, ghosts were more static than mortals because they lacked animal souls (the things that become hungry ghosts) to keep them dynamic. Now, 3e may move away from the Hun/P'o paradigm of Eastern philosophy, but I think that would disrespect the contributions of Eastern philosophy to Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:33:34-07:00","id":888518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888315#post888315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I hate the suggestion that Infernals should be inherently evil with no moral agency or free will, I also want Abyssals to have moral agency, and the power to tell the Neverborn and Deathlords to suck it and become antiheroes. Let people tell that story about Abyssals if they want it. It isn't going to make evil loyalist Abyssals disappear if others go renegade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is also facilitated by making the Deathlords more complex characters than &quot;Ghost who sold out for power and now wants the world destroyed.&quot; If the Deathlords have motives more complex than simply killing Creation, a vast expanse of narrative space appears.<br /> <br /> You could even run a GoT-style game where the Abyssals politic, intrigue, and betray their masters for new ones while the Deathlords themselves match wits and wills in a centuries-long game.<br /> <br /> And then of course some bright enterprising Abyssal realizes they don't require the patronage of the Deathlords, and things get interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T15:29:51-07:00","id":888614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888382#post888382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least according to previous editions, ghosts were more static than mortals because they lacked animal souls (the things that become hungry ghosts) to keep them dynamic. Now, 3e may move away from the Hun/P'o paradigm of Eastern philosophy, but I think that would disrespect the contributions of Eastern philosophy to Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hungry ghosts are still the Po souls of mortals - we have it in the example hungry ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T15:55:44-07:00","id":888635,"title":"","content":"I agree with the idea of Abyssals getting more agency, and better room for the option of &quot;what if I don't want to work for the Thirteen Ghosts of Scooby-Doo&quot; to breathe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:21:23-07:00","id":890642,"title":"","content":"On the subject of ghosts:<br /> <br /> \u200bI just watched a video of the last five or so minutes of My Dinner with Andre, in which the title character actually uses the term &quot;ghost&quot; to refer to how mysterious and unreachable other people are, especially as you become closer to them and thus have more opportunities to be aware of how little you really know them. It's actually part of a longer dialogue concerning awareness and experience of death, which may also be relevant but that I won't go into here, but it was interesting to me because it touches on a subject I'm fascinated by in general, and have sometimes considered as a basis for considering and portraying ghosts (and Fair Folk). The notion that what it might functionally mean for ghosts to be without one of their souls is that there might be very little of them there beyond what you see on the surface, but this doesn't necessarily detract from relating to them, because that might be the only level at which you ever relate to anybody; it might matter more as a basis for their actions independent of relating to others.<br /> <br /> There can be granularity to that, such that maybe only the very most insignificant and weak ghosts actually present it as being completely repetitive of some living daily routine and largely unaware of their surroundings. That most have a level of depth that could be sufficient to have some decent relationship with them for a while (with just how long depending on who you are as well; there are probably people who could get by their entire lives with a relationship in which they never really know the other person). That's short of the most advanced ghosts, the ones who could be said to have enough substance to realise what they're lacking and try to fill it in by maintaining connections with and the prominence of things from their memories, or retaining ties to living relatives and others who can provide them with fleeting substance of blood and memory, and ultimately live vicariously for them.<br /> <br /> The alternative being ghosts who, with the absence of such things (or having finally lost them all to time), fill themselves out with what they can draw from the other direction. The Deathlords being the most powerful and sophisticated of these.<br /> <br /> In some of those senses, I feel as though it's possible to treat Deathlords with some depth and nuance, even sympathy, even if they're all still characterised as ultimately hating the living, or at least having fearsome designs on them.<br /> <br /> I would be interested if these could be things significant to Abyssals regardless of their directions, regardless of how much personal investment and loyalty they can have towards the figures who have a lot of experience and teaching to provide them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:55:27-07:00","id":890691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalad2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888294#post888294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want abyssals to be world slaying apocalypse weapons loyal to Oblivion, none of this romance of the grave or deathly honor or ghost king nonsense</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got Nephwracks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:02:56-07:00","id":890695,"title":"","content":"I want to say that, in previous editions, ghosts were just collections of thought and memory, empty of the passion of real people. However, given how often ghost stories seem to be about passion, either good or bad, I wonder if that's the correct route to take. Alternately, maybe some Hungry Ghosts can retain a certain amount of sentience, at least enough such that those stories can be told.<br /> <br /> Also, why are some ghosts &quot;more powerful&quot; than others? Is it just due to them having a cult or embracing Oblivion? Is it an inherent property of their soul? Does it relate to how they died? Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:36:29-07:00","id":890801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=890695#post890695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why are some ghosts &quot;more powerful&quot; than others? Is it just due to them having a cult or embracing Oblivion? Is it an inherent property of their soul? Does it relate to how they died? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't one fixed path to power for ghosts. The Deathlords are mighty, but they didn't all reach the height of their power in exactly the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T17:55:04-07:00","id":890884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=890801#post890801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't one fixed path to power for ghosts. The Deathlords are mighty, but they didn't all reach the height of their power in exactly the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm reminded a bit of one of the well known Masquer assassin (shaping ghosts corpus) NPCs, Slander. In one story that's a vision of a bad future, it's revealed that there are like 7-8 other Slanders who will continue on. No one knows what Slander looked like, because they can look like anything, and when there's multiple of them and no one knows FOR SURE which killings they did... that's one thing I like because it's something ghosts can pull off that'd be far harder for an Exalt (or 8 in this case). I think ghosts can be powerful, but in ways that are VERY DIFFERENT from any Exalted. It's not quite the sideways thing that Sids had in previous editions, but more 10 steps while staying in place, then leaping forward.<br /> <br /> Also, it strikes me that one of the paths should be a &quot;stage identity&quot;... like instead of hiding their name, they create a false persona that people believe in and talk about. Their beliefs lend it power, but only in ways that support the persona's nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T23:25:04-07:00","id":891010,"title":"","content":"Make Abyssals (and Infernals) different from Solars. No mirror Charms. Downplay/rework/discard the &quot;Stolen Solar Exaltations&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> Talk more about the Metaphysics that created the Neverborn, and reflect those mechanisms in Abyssal/ghost Charms/Necromancy.<br /> <br /> Give us likable Deathlords - someone that doesn't immediately set out to destroy the world, but can be a potential ally,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:22:43-07:00","id":891113,"title":"","content":"I think Abyssals should be more connected to ghosts, and Liminals more connected to corpses.<br /> <br /> As to whether a ghost is a person or not: in Buddhism, a sentient being is composed of five <b>Skandha</b>, aggregate functions that arise as a result of our existence. Material form, feelings, perceptions, volitions, and senses continuously begin and end, and as such, there is no real self, no real &quot;I.&quot;<br /> <br /> So hypothetically, in Creation, when a person dies, their Skandha are disconnected. Some are housed in the Hun, in the Po, and in the corpse. And many of these are a components of a human, and to say that they aren't human is to say that our moonlight isn't also our sunlight. So a ghost is human, but not a <i>complete</i> human, possessing several but not all Skandha. If self is an illusion, then with a ghost the illusion grows even more dim.<br /> <br /> However, there's a big difference between knowing something and really internalizing it. I have accepted that I have no self, that &quot;I&quot; does not exist, but it's very difficult to keep in mind at all times, as I have to use personal nominative pronouns like &quot;I&quot; to interact with others. As such, characters may academically act clinically to a ghost, but <i>react</i> very differently because it tugs at their intimacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T02:15:40-07:00","id":891633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalad2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=888332#post888332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't find &quot;end the world&quot; to be an interesting campaign goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's this chinese take out place, Chef Lee's, about a minutes drive from my house. Whenever I go there, I ask for the orange chicken, because they make them some damn fine orange chicken. There's a decent sized menu, the usual suspects of Beef, Pork, Chicken, Buddhist Vegetarian, your typical chinese cuisine, but Orange Chicken is my favorite, and if you're going to eat you, you might as well eat your favorite, especially when it's at a place that makes it so good.<br /> <br /> It could be the very best orange chicken in the world. But if it only served orange chicken, it'd make for a pretty lousy restaurant.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:19:09-07:00","id":891649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891633#post891633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your typical chinese cuisine could be the very best orange chicken in the world. But if it only served orange chicken, it'd make for a pretty lousy restaurant.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>haha there's no such thing as typical chinese cuisine. It's always typical province cuisines and there's thousands of dishes. I for one have yet to encounter orange chicken so far, and i've been living for 5 years in Beijing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T04:18:45-07:00","id":891665,"title":"","content":"It's a given that any &quot;Chinese food&quot; you get in America is actually &quot;American food,&quot; typically not even cleverly disguised. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Fortune cookie, anyone?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Still, while a solid nitpick, the point's still pretty solid: Abyssals would be pretty shitty if all they ever did was destroy the world or start out destroying the world but then rebel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:14:22-07:00","id":891673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891649#post891649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">haha there's no such thing as typical chinese cuisine. It's always typical province cuisines and there's thousands of dishes. I for one have yet to encounter orange chicken so far, and i've been living for 5 years in Beijing</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried not eating out of trash cans?<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>-That was uncalled for. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-16-2016, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:56:26-07:00","id":891682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891673#post891673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried not eating out of trash cans?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>meh... most american-chinese food is inspired by hong kong/southern china food. Not much of that up north","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T06:53:56-07:00","id":891706,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's no Dong-Bei food in the west. I'm going to miss my Go Ba Ro.<br /> <br /> But we should probably get back to Abyssals. Yeah, destroying the world/rebelling against the Deathlords was kind of dull. I mean, it's fine for one or two characters, but after that...<br /> For the first couple of years of running a Solar/Lunar game, I used Walker in Darkness (with a side of Mask of Winters) as the main antagonist, and honestly his Abyssals-of-the-week got a bit dull. I mean, they weren't very memorable when they were just all people trying to destroy the world. The only more memorable one... was the one who was rebelling against the Deathlords and worked with the PCs.<br /> I literally swore to never use Abyssals as the main antagonists again, I got so bored of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:21:53-07:00","id":891718,"title":"","content":"I found that the classic setup really made the Deathlords the main antagonists and the actual Solar dark reflections (normally by being a PCs previous incarnation to draw obvious parallels) while the default Abyssal characterisation made their contrast to Solars a shallow inversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:34:24-07:00","id":891723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891718#post891718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found that the classic setup really made the Deathlords the main antagonists and the actual Solar dark reflections (normally by being a PCs previous incarnation to draw obvious parallels)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about focusing on the Deathlords more as ambiguous guide and instructor figures, like a shadow in the distance who points things out to Abyssals, is what made me start to consider the merits of some as them not being the ghosts of Solars.<br /> <br /> What you've stated here is an additional merit to the idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:57:22-07:00","id":891731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891723#post891723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about focusing on the Deathlords more as ambiguous guide and instructor figures, like a shadow in the distance who points things out to Abyssals, is what made me start to consider the merits of some as them not being the ghosts of Solars.<br /> <br /> What you've stated here is an additional merit to the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like the sky opened up in my head.<br /> <br /> Deathlords NOT as Solar ghosts? Deathlords as just really powerful ghosts; any ghost might become a Deathlord, even the ghosts of the unExalted?<br /> <br /> It's not like this would give Abyssals access to Sidereal-like magic through Sidereal ghosts, either, since the Sidereal Deathlord can only approximate his former abilities through the lens of ghostly Underworld power.<br /> <br /> And because ghostly power will still be different from Solar power even for the Solar ghosts, the Abyssals will still be closer to mirroring the Solar Exalted than any Solar ghost Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:00:16-07:00","id":891735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891731#post891731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like the sky opened up in my head.<br /> <br /> Deathlords NOT as Solar ghosts? Deathlords as just really powerful ghosts; any ghost might become a Deathlord, even the ghosts of the unExalted?<br /> <br /> It's not like this would give Abyssals access to Sidereal-like magic through Sidereal ghosts, either, since the Sidereal Deathlord can only approximate his former abilities through the lens of ghostly Underworld power.<br /> <br /> And because ghostly power will still be different from Solar power even for the Solar ghosts, the Abyssals will still be closer to mirroring the Solar Exalted than any Solar ghost Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Since this idea was breached I've had so many deathlord concepts. None of whom wish to end the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-16-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:03:45-07:00","id":891736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891113#post891113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Abyssals should be more connected to ghosts, and Liminals more connected to corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are restless by definition, in Creation. Corpses are immobile objects.<br /> <br /> Animated corpses are by far the EXCEPTION in Creation, and generally always the work of ghosts, Abyssals (who you suggest would be affiliated with ghosts), people who create more Liminals (which aren't the concern of other Liminals), and possibly sorcerers.<br /> <br /> It's hard to tell how often sorcerers bother with animating corpses -- there's no spell for it in the corebook, there's no Necromancy initiation as such, and any sorcerer can learn a single spell to create any elemental they can imagine or summon any demon that exists (and which the player can imagine).<br /> <br /> So, I doubt this is a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:10:35-07:00","id":891740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891735#post891735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Since this idea was breach I've had so many deathlord concepts. None of whom wish to end the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes the Underworld so much more organic and malleable.<br /> <br /> Not only is the Underworld fragmented into multiple different kinds of afterlives, heavens, and hells, but Deathlords might arise and fall at any time through natural selection and luck? You could actually build a few of your own interesting places within the Underworld!<br /> <br /> It's not like the Wyld, either. You have an extremely reasonable chance of returning to those places later and finding them largely unchanged and waiting for your further interactions, especially BECAUSE ghosts generally don't change or grow. If anything happened in your absence, it's probably because of some Plot Hook that occurred while you were gone, or it's because of the changes you started before you left.<br /> <br /> That's cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, without knowing the exact details of what a Deathlord is or how a ghost becomes one, right now there exists the amusing possibility that Deathlord is BOTH one of the Soul Reapers of <i>Bleach </i>AND one of the Vasto Lordes. But with various methods of becoming a Deathlord, we can definitely have Soul Reapers <i>and </i>Vasto Lordes duking it out in the afterlife, with Soul Society and Hueco Mundo being two zones of the Underworld separated by the rivers of death.<br /> <br /> Actually, this begs for another name. If Lethe is being reused for the concept/condition of reincarnation/forgetfulness, then perhaps the Acheron for the condition of each distinct zone being separated by surreality?<br /> <br /> The Styx could be twin of Lethe; a poetic term for the condition of dying in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:31:21-07:00","id":891755,"title":"","content":"If there are more than 13 Deathlords, like a hundred of them, they need to be vastly, vastly, vastly less powerful than in previous editions, or even weaker than Abyssals, to prevent them from overwhelming Creation. I'm very leery of creating an uncapped number of better-than-Exalted superbeings, especially if in 3E they're powerful enough to create their own Exalted instead of the Neverborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:43:12-07:00","id":891762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891755#post891755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are more than 13 Deathlords, like a hundred of them, they need to be vastly, vastly, vastly less powerful than in previous editions, or even weaker than Abyssals, to prevent them from overwhelming Creation. I'm very leery of creating an uncapped number of better-than-Exalted superbeings, especially if in 3E they're powerful enough to create their own Exalted instead of the Neverborn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was envisioning something no more (and likely much less) numerous than Terrestrial Exalted, and possibly of comparable power.<br /> <br /> Like, a Deathlord of sufficient experience could be a danger to an Abyssal of insufficient experience, especially when hitting outside of the Exalt's competencies, but the intent is always that a Dusk Caste can rapidly rise to the point where he can choose to overthrow his mentor, the First and Forsaken Lion, in order to take over his armies and start his OWN campaign across the Deadlands.<br /> <br /> The Dusk Caste might need the help of his Abyssal Circle to do it, but players have Circles by default.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I wasn't thinking that Deathlords would create Abyssals. Abyssals are still corrupted Solar Exaltations. HOW they got into the Underworld and into the hands of powerful ghosts is something I almost don't even care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:44:04-07:00","id":891763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891755#post891755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are more than 13 Deathlords, like a hundred of them, they need to be vastly, vastly, vastly less powerful than in previous editions, or even weaker than Abyssals, to prevent them from overwhelming Creation. I'm very leery of creating an uncapped number of godlike beings powerful enough to create their own Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We can have 13 powerful deathlords and maybe a bunch of death barons? One of my deathlord ideas is a low level death Baron that controls a Shadowland on the Blessed Isle. The Realm hasn't stamped out this Deathlord yet, because they have been very helpful and the deathlord has a lot of allies among the Dynasts on the Isle.<br /> <br /> Also, an ST can kick one of the thirteen out of the setting and make their own custom deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:46:17-07:00","id":891766,"title":"","content":"Um, Erinys, you can stop beating that drum now. We've already heard that the devs have no intention of making the Deathlords continue the 2e line of being Essence 10 Double Exalt Ghostatonkhires. <br /> <br /> <i>Nobody</i> is gonna be <i>that</i> powerful in Ex3 because the intention is that no one is so powerful that they can't be challenged. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind, though, that doesn't stop them from being terrifyingly powerful or dangerous - after all, so are Second Circle Demons, high-end gods, elemental dragons, Fair Folk nobles, Third Circle Demons, the Incarnae, that big weird turtle that holds four elephants on its back, and of course the Exalted themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:21:38-07:00","id":891798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891763#post891763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, an ST can kick one of the thirteen out of the setting and make their own custom deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're probably going to keep the &quot;9 of which described in the supplements&quot; thing from Ex2.<br /> <br /> Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 05-16-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:22:09-07:00","id":891799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891736#post891736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I doubt this is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a statement I'm wary of because there's still plenty of room for an Abyssal to be a necrosurgeon that's constantly grave robbing to modify their own body, but the critical difference between them and a Liminal is that they chose to be this thing.<br /> <br /> Much like how they could be a face-stealing serial killer in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:55:46-07:00","id":891822,"title":"","content":"So, for example, the Lover Clad in Raiment of Tears is the ghost of a Solar who made afterlife bargains for increased power until she seduced and consumed a Hekkatonkhire, becoming a Deathlord. While the Silver Prince is actually &quot;just&quot; a charlatan-sorcerer who built a cult to himself as the Bodhissatva, and through nurturing what amounts to a glorified ancestor cult, fed himself on enormous power until his powerful necromancy allowed his ghost to tap into a well of power beyond the Labyrinth, and rise as the &quot;resurrected&quot; Silver Prince according to his own prophecy. The Eye and Seven Despairs, meanwhile, is a ghost-blooded Lunar Half Caste who never quite died, but whose obsessions with intrigue outweighed his strength of will and led him to a rich fantasy life of a small horde of false faces, some of which have forgotten they ever were false, and has sought meaning in nihilistic revenge cycles that brought him to the attention of the Deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:23:33-07:00","id":891844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891798#post891798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're probably going to keep the &quot;9 of which described in the supplements&quot; thing from Ex2.<br /> <br /> Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't remember if all 13 slots were filled with Canon characters or not. <br /> <br /> The ST answer is &quot;which ever Death Lord is in the area of Creation the game is set in.&quot; If I am running a game in the North, the Bishop or the Lover is getting the whack. <br /> <br /> In general? The Lover is my least favorite death Lord. (We joke nick named her &quot;Sexy Mask of Winters&quot; in a Ex2 game I played in.) The reasons why I dislike her could derail a thread and ignite a flame war. So I will just say I hope they flesh her out in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:10:38-07:00","id":891868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891844#post891844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I will just say I hope they flesh her out in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, man, don't you think she's fleshy <i>enough</i>?!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:13:09-07:00","id":891870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891844#post891844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I will just say I hope they <b>flesh her out </b>in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>*rimshot* Thank you ladies and gentlemen, I'll be here all week!<br /> <br /> ****Jeez, Alucard beat me to it handily.!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:17:57-07:00","id":891876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891731#post891731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any ghost might become a Deathlord</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bIt's funny, I think &quot;any X might become super-Y&quot; is a distinction people only really seem to note when a setting already contains, or is predicated on, people who have power bestowed or inborn or whatever in some way.<br /> <br /> You get fictions in which some individual is demonstrably talented or remarkable in some manner, often pivotal, but when it's on its own it doesn't seem to be worth commenting on at all, let alone as some kind of equalizing point.<br /> <br /> I just thought of this while wondering about why I might disagree with the idea applied to Deathlords, and it made me wonder if the distinction really means anything.<br /> <br /> I suppose with the Exalted, it might ruffle some people because of an approximate limit being set on them, but...<br /> <br /> Heh, is it too much for me to assume that if nobody ever stated anything like a limit to the Exalted, and/or an idea that they were something that happened because of divine favour, most people would just default to acting as though there were about ten of them? <br /> <br /> I'm just making a stray observation, I'm sure Sunder's point is meant to read as &quot;a Deathlord might be a ghost of any category&quot; rather than a statement on the ultimate potential of every ghost.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:03:19-07:00","id":891904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891876#post891876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just making a stray observation, I'm sure Sunder's point is meant to read as &quot;a Deathlord might be a ghost of any category&quot; rather than a statement on the ultimate potential of every ghost.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. We are talking about Deathlords coming from more diverse backgrounds than &quot;Angry Solar Ghost&quot;. I don't want every ghost to the potential to become a Deathlord, but rather a Deathlord could have started out as a ghost of any origin. Just because Genghis Khan was human doesn't mean every human can become Genghis Khan. There is only enough room for so many crazy dictator types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:51:13-07:00","id":892032,"title":"","content":"Yes, I wasn't talking about a universal potential, but rather the idea that a Deathlord can arise from any kind of ghost. Maybe the ghosts of an unExalted mortal has to work harder, or a non-Solar ghost has to jump through more (or simply different!) hoops than a Solar ghost, but they can have any sort of impressive background rather than one specific origin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, all of the known and proposed and theorized changes make it much easier to have Saigyouji Yuyuko as a relatively benevolent (if pathologically cryptic) Deathlord of the Hakugyokuro (Tower of White Jade) deadland/Shadowland populated by ghosts of artists and poets, guarded by the Konpaku clan of Ghost-Blooded warriors, who count among their number Konpaku Youmu, Dusk Caste Abyssal Exalt and student of Single Point Shining Into The Void Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:01:16-07:00","id":892040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=892032#post892032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, all of the known and proposed and theorized changes make it much easier to have Saigyouji Yuyuko as a relatively benevolent (if pathologically cryptic) Deathlord of the Hakugyokuro (Tower of White Jade) deadland/Shadowland populated by ghosts of artists and poets, guarded by the Konpaku clan of Ghost-Blooded warriors, who count among their number Konpaku Youmu, Dusk Caste Abyssal Exalt and student of Single Point Shining Into The Void Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been crypt about it, but my deathlord idea involves artists and crafters and the like. Basically artists flock to the deathlord because the deathlord's students ending producing the greatest works. Of course these students usually burn out and die within a year of so of entering the shadowland. But they will &quot;live&quot; on through their art. <br /> <br /> I'll need to read more about the Tower of White Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:14:01-07:00","id":892052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=892040#post892040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been crypt about it, but my deathlord idea involves artists and crafters and the like. Basically artists flock to the deathlord because the deathlord's students ending producing the greatest works. Of course these students usually burn out and die within a year of so of entering the shadowland. But they will &quot;live&quot; on through their art.<br /> <br /> I'll need to read more about the Tower of White Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a mythical place in Japanese folklore, related to a real place where various artists died or frequently committed suicide or something.<br /> <br /> In Touhou, the namesake tower is rarely if ever seen; far more attention is given to the sprawling garden of sakura trees that Youmu tends, using her ridiculous speed to reach from one end to the other, pruning with her paired swords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:18:39-07:00","id":893237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891798#post891798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a doubt, the Lover as she is now. I have no interest to deal with her. She just feels like a congealed mass of bad and overused tropes. I feel like the old Abyssal idea preview made it abundantly clear she's a problem.<br /> <br /> If they do her a billion times better, well that could be ok. But as things are, nope. I can't think of anyone I know who used a very canon version of her well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:46:11-07:00","id":893258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891798#post891798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bHmmmm... it <i>used</i> to be the Walker in Darkness, but between John's description of a new form of him as a kind of terrifying romantic mercenary lord and the description of Narasen in Death's Master selling me more on the whole blue skin image, I'm more attached to his possibilities.<br /> <br /> So at the moment, I suppose... Eye and Seven Despairs?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:28:38-07:00","id":893288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893237#post893237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a doubt, the Lover as she is now. I have no interest to deal with her. She just feels like a congealed mass of bad and overused tropes. I feel like the old Abyssal idea preview made it abundantly clear she's a problem.<br /> <br /> If they do her a billion times better, well that could be ok. But as things are, nope. I can't think of anyone I know who used a very canon version of her well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canon Lover is terrifying antagonist. Most people (including rival Deathlords) just look at the &quot;orgies! orgies! rape!&quot; part, which is pretty much what she wants as written:<br /> &quot;Only the Bodhisattva does not share that view, for he remembers the Lover from their living days. Remembers her and fears her. For the Lover, when she bore a different name and served the Unconquered Sun, ventured into the Labyrinth before any of the other future Deathlords even knew what it was.&quot; She is probably most cunning of all Deathlords, as she plays the long game and utilize constant Xanathos Gambits - shown with Warstrider she &quot;gifted&quot; to Lookshy.<br /> She is the master of intrigue among the Deathlords, she can put a price on every soul. She is the most powerful or at least, second most powerful necromancer among Deathlords. And probably most scary of them all - &quot;Among all the Deathlords, only the Lover does not seek revenge on Creation for her betrayal and murder. Quite the contrary, she feels grateful that the Dragon-Blooded ended her banal excuse for a life, and she hopes to honor their heroism by returning the favor. Convinced of the utter pointlessness of human existence, the Lover spreads ultimate pleasure among her followers because she knows from bitter experience that when pleasure ends, nothing of any value remains.&quot;<br /> <br /> At this moment, the Deathlord I would certainly remove is Prince with his doomsday fleet (he was much better in 1st edition without that fleet, but probably was considered not enough threat) or Dowager with her sudden and instant &quot;destroy all&quot; option (she is however very interesting narratively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T08:03:49-07:00","id":893311,"title":"","content":"For me, I'd say the Dowager, because I don't see that you'd get much in the way of interesting stories out of her as a Deathlord. Other than &quot;oh, she's found another plague to decimate Creation&quot; which you could have any of the others do anyway.<br /> <br /> As a powerful and insane necro-witch who lives in a marsh, sure, that's fine. But there's no need to be a Deathlord for that (unless of course, you radically change what a Deathlord is... which they might well do).<br /> <br /> I do feel that Walker in Darkness is the blandest and most generic of all the Deathlords. But hey, probably some people want a generic Deathlord, and he delivers nicely.<br /> I do like his dog though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T09:30:49-07:00","id":893383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891798#post891798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're probably going to keep the &quot;9 of which described in the supplements&quot; thing from Ex2.<br /> <br /> Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. I would make more. Basic problem of having a stable of DBBs: nature can't take its course without someone feeling cheated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:04:58-07:00","id":893403,"title":"","content":"So people are saying the Underworld has radically changed and no longer looks like a map of Creation.<br /> Is it less similar to the Wraith Underworld now, or more similar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T10:06:06-07:00","id":893406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=891798#post891798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, minor thread drift, If you could write off one Deathlord, which one would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mannfred von Carstein. The asshole basically caused Warhammer Fantasy Battle to become Age of Sigmar which seemed like a decent way to end his story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:01:28-07:00","id":893442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893258#post893258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHmmmm... it <i>used</i> to be the Walker in Darkness, but between John's description of a new form of him as a kind of terrifying romantic mercenary lord and the description of Narasen in Death's Master selling me more on the whole blue skin image, I'm more attached to his possibilities.<br /> <br /> So at the moment, I suppose... Eye and Seven Despairs?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always thought of Walker in Darkness more by his other title of Psychopomp. It made me think he was focused more on the Underworld, and cared very little for the living unless they were causing problems for the dead. He was there to help the dead find their place and grow and eventually move on. This isn't to say he couldn't be terrifying. Imagine someone who is doing something horrible, but doesn't realize how terrible it is, and actually is a GOOD PERSON with an unfortunate lack of insight on what he's doing. A likeable and not antagonistic Deathlord? It's got potential, even while the PCs might want to oppose him. Sometimes the best villains are good people who fail to see the bad results in their good intentions. I thought it could all go well with his lack of memory. He doesn't have the spite the others do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893403#post893403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So people are saying the Underworld has radically changed and no longer looks like a map of Creation.<br /> Is it less similar to the Wraith Underworld now, or more similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's tough to answer but... probably more like Wraith. The Shadowlands was one layer, but the game had important stuff going on in the Tempest, which held NOTHING of Earth, except for things built there to look like it... oh and one vampire city that got nuked away. I don't know if there should be a Tempest layer, BUT... I think some of the elements from it could fit well into the Underworld of Exalted. Now certain areas are held stable through ritual, or amusingly Shadowlands provide a stability even beyond their borders. But what about the more wild areas? Maybe they're a wild sea, or a storm-blasted area unlike anything in Creation. That's something that feels like it could be great. &quot;These areas are like Creation in shape... but the others? They're dangerous to linger in without some sort of protection.&quot; Which actually offers something positive for social things there. There are REASONS rebels might hide in those areas. Maybe they've made a little safer fort and ways to get in and out. But then the dangers outside become defenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:02:30-07:00","id":893444,"title":"","content":"As long as we don't have a blanket statement of the deathlords having &quot;every solars charms&quot;....I will be happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:52:18-07:00","id":893500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893442#post893442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's tough to answer but... probably more like Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a huge fan of Wraith. It was deeply flawed as a game but had such an exquisitely baroque setting and tragic, heartbreaking themes that I can't help but have an abiding fondness for it. The old 2E hardback was the only RPG book that I would actually pick up and read for pleasure before I encountered Exalted back in First Edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't draw direct parallels from Wraith for the Underworld of Exalted any more than I would want the Scavenger Lands to look like Greyhawk - it's <i>always </i>better for a setting to be its own thing rather than an imitation of something else. But that doesn't mean we can't borrow inspiration where it's available.<ul><li>The Tempest need not be a separate dimension/layer, but the idea of Maelstrom-like storms sweeping across the new geography of the Underworld with howling, Oblivion-wracked specters carried on their winds is too breathtakingly awful not to include. It would also serve to help explain why the Underworld isn't just a boring landscape filled with aimless ghosts - the unquiet shades of the dead gather together in enclaves and cities for mutual protection and build bulwarks to protect them against the dangers of their world, just as the living do. Not just storms, but hekatonkhires, ghostly beasts like anglerfish that lurk to swallow the unwary soul entire, marauding bands of renegades and slaver-wraiths that prey on those too weak to oppose them, and other weirder things. The Underworld ought to be at least as strange and dangerous as Creation, but in a totally different way.</li> <li>The Hierarchy might not map directly on to the Underworld as a whole, but it could make a beautifully oppressive framework for a given Domain - perhaps one ruled by a Deathlord, but not necessarily - where the unquiet shades must struggle to find productive work or demand burnt offerings from their own descendents so that they can pay their annual tithe to the patrolling Legionnaries. If they fail, they face a forfeit which can mean being maimed, enslaved, or even forged. These ghosts might struggle under the weight of their obligation, but at least they are safe from the dangers that prowl the untamed lands beyond their borders.</li> <li>Ancient cities from the Shogunate or earlier that exist only as forgotten ruins in Creation might have fallen entirely into the Underworld. Some might have been consumed by the Labyrinth, but others might still persist in some strange fashion, even exerting their own mnemonic gravity on the malleable world around them to shape weird not-quite-right islands of being that almost resemble what they once were, before they were not any longer.</li> <li>In a setting like this, the Abyssals can be so much more than just sad angry emo vampires. They can be heralds of Oblivion, sure. But they can also be the champions who rally the souls of the Dead to the wall, throwing back the hungry tide of night and lighting the lanterns that hold it at bay. They can be the emissaries who walk fearlessly between the lands of the dead and the living, or who cross the dark waters from one Domain to another to carry news and forge treaties and reunite the souls of loved ones thought lost forever. They can be the creators and arbiters of the Laws of the Dead which prevent a ghostly city from succumbing to corruption, despair and dissolution in the face of the insidious rot of the Nephwracks and their doppleganger spies. They can be the curators of knowledge that has gone from Creation but still echoes in the forgotten halls of fallen empires, delving into those secret places and carrying back what was thought lost. They can be the hunters of great beasts that even when slain refuse to die. They can do more than just play at heroism, they can <i>actually be heroic</i>.</li> </ul><br /> I certainly hope the Underworld delivers something like this, because that's what I want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:55:38-07:00","id":893576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893444#post893444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we don't have a blanket statement of the deathlords having &quot;every solars charms&quot;....I will be happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will be happy. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:00:12-07:00","id":893640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893500#post893500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a huge fan of Wraith. It was deeply flawed as a game but had such an exquisitely baroque setting and tragic, heartbreaking themes that I can't help but have an abiding fondness for it. The old 2E hardback was the only RPG book that I would actually pick up and read for pleasure before I encountered Exalted back in First Edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't draw direct parallels from Wraith for the Underworld of Exalted any more than I would want the Scavenger Lands to look like Greyhawk - it's <i>always </i>better for a setting to be its own thing rather than an imitation of something else. But that doesn't mean we can't borrow inspiration where it's available.<ul><li>The Tempest need not be a separate dimension/layer, but the idea of Maelstrom-like storms sweeping across the new geography of the Underworld with howling, Oblivion-wracked specters carried on their winds is too breathtakingly awful not to include. It would also serve to help explain why the Underworld isn't just a boring landscape filled with aimless ghosts - the unquiet shades of the dead gather together in enclaves and cities for mutual protection and build bulwarks to protect them against the dangers of their world, just as the living do. Not just storms, but hekatonkhires, ghostly beasts like anglerfish that lurk to swallow the unwary soul entire, marauding bands of renegades and slaver-wraiths that prey on those too weak to oppose them, and other weirder things. The Underworld ought to be at least as strange and dangerous as Creation, but in a totally different way.</li> <li>The Hierarchy might not map directly on to the Underworld as a whole, but it could make a beautifully oppressive framework for a given Domain - perhaps one ruled by a Deathlord, but not necessarily - where the unquiet shades must struggle to find productive work or demand burnt offerings from their own descendents so that they can pay their annual tithe to the patrolling Legionnaries. If they fail, they face a forfeit which can mean being maimed, enslaved, or even forged. These ghosts might struggle under the weight of their obligation, but at least they are safe from the dangers that prowl the untamed lands beyond their borders.</li> <li>Ancient cities from the Shogunate or earlier that exist only as forgotten ruins in Creation might have fallen entirely into the Underworld. Some might have been consumed by the Labyrinth, but others might still persist in some strange fashion, even exerting their own mnemonic gravity on the malleable world around them to shape weird not-quite-right islands of being that almost resemble what they once were, before they were not any longer.</li> <li>In a setting like this, the Abyssals can be so much more than just sad angry emo vampires. They can be heralds of Oblivion, sure. But they can also be the champions who rally the souls of the Dead to the wall, throwing back the hungry tide of night and lighting the lanterns that hold it at bay. They can be the emissaries who walk fearlessly between the lands of the dead and the living, or who cross the dark waters from one Domain to another to carry news and forge treaties and reunite the souls of loved ones thought lost forever. They can be the creators and arbiters of the Laws of the Dead which prevent a ghostly city from succumbing to corruption, despair and dissolution in the face of the insidious rot of the Nephwracks and their doppleganger spies. They can be the curators of knowledge that has gone from Creation but still echoes in the forgotten halls of fallen empires, delving into those secret places and carrying back what was thought lost. They can be the hunters of great beasts that even when slain refuse to die. They can do more than just play at heroism, they can <i>actually be heroic</i>.</li> </ul><br /> I certainly hope the Underworld delivers something like this, because that's what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is EXACTLY what I was thinking. Like don't take things EXACTLY, but you can incorporate aspects that would work. I think Renegades work well, because let's be honest. There's always going to be SOMEONE not happy with the current status quo. So it's not so much a Wraith only thing. Like the only thing I think I'd use super closely is Doomslayers for the Labyrinth stuff (and some things about specters that adds more spice and variety). Yes, totally do ancient cities and such. In fact, why not have a library of lost knowledge? Stuff that was carelessly destroyed in Creation, preserved by ghosts who care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:32:20-07:00","id":893670,"title":"","content":"One notable thing brought up in the new edition is that Ex3's Underworld is no longer &quot;Creation, but in grayscale and with ghosts.&quot; In fact, some parts of it are <i>more</i> colorful than its Creation counterpart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:53:51-07:00","id":893754,"title":"","content":"I'd be comfortable with about 91 Deathlords, commanding legions of Nephwracks and Hecatonchires. And then I'd contrast them between Heaven, Malfeas, the Wyld, and Creation in terms of organization, agency, reach, and raw power. Hell and the Underworld have more then enough raw power to retake Creation, but fold to Heaven's reach, the Wyld's agency, and Creation's organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:01:54-07:00","id":893840,"title":"","content":"An Underworld where Abyssals can actually be genuinely heroic sounds great.<br /> I hope the Dual Monarchy and the kingdom they ruled, set up in the First Age to hold out against Oblivion, is still a thing though.<br /> <br /> Man the Underworld sucks though. In all editions. Why do ghosts hang around instead of going to Lethe? Did the Great Contagion &quot;break&quot; it so that's almost impossible now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:14:24-07:00","id":893844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893840#post893840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do ghosts hang around instead of going to Lethe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some folks, bafflingly to me, prefer existence to nonexistence. I'd be the first one to cannonball into lethe/oblivion/whatever. Ghosts tend not to be people like me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:33:01-07:00","id":893847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893840#post893840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the Dual Monarchy and the kingdom they ruled, set up in the First Age to hold out against Oblivion, is still a thing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dual Monarchy is one of the only things about the Underworld in 2e that I liked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:43:15-07:00","id":893920,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;Lethe and Oblivion are equivalent&quot; thing is something that's been on my mind ever since I've read a few things that made me think about the nature of memory and personality and how they're not quite as equivalent as people have tended to suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T03:13:23-07:00","id":893931,"title":"","content":"I don't mind if some players, with their western 21st century mind-sets, think that they are the same, it's good to have things to debate... but considering how many seem to, it perhaps needs to more clear that people in the setting generally don't think it's the same. I wouldn't mind if characters in Exalted had a particular reason to think so (like, say, people meditating and seeing visions of their past lives), though I don't think it's necessary. But maybe that's just because it seems obvious to me that they wouldn't think of it the same way, and others seem to disagree.<br /> <br /> Of course, Oblivion may be a bit different in this edition anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-19-2016, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T04:10:16-07:00","id":893936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893931#post893931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind if some players, with their western 21st century mind-sets think that they are the same</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou mean the mindset that includes things like neurology and conditioning? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let me ask you a question; what is your favourite food?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T04:30:44-07:00","id":893940,"title":"","content":"It's changed over time. These days I don't really have one. Where are you going with this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:01:23-07:00","id":893947,"title":"","content":"Okay, just a thing that you particularly enjoy consuming because of its flavour.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat is the basis of favoured tastes? The series of synaptic responses that provoke a positive association with consuming a particular thing. The conditioned or genetically coded circuitry that connects the relevant parts of your brain?<br /> <br /> Is it memory? Is there an event in your life that you remember that makes a thing desirable to taste, that compels one particularly towards it? If you like the taste of fudge above all other sweets, would that cease to be the case even if you were made to forget what fudge even was?<br /> <br /> Do you have habits? Do you have emotional patterns? Consistent cognitive processes? Muscle memory?<br /> <br /> Things that largely arise from how chemicals and electrical impulses are shunted around the particular architecture of your brain?<br /> <br /> If you had no memories, a lot of that would remain. A lot of your impulses, what attracts and repels, how one responds, would remain consistent. You might not recognise anybody else, but there can be a fair amount by which others can recognise you.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the reincarnated soul might not be a seat for those patterns. That a person who lives long enough to see the same soul over multiple lifetimes exhibit many of the same traits that have little or nothing to do with procedural memory. Maybe continuously make the same positive contributions. Maybe gradually transition away from bad habits as altered environments add new layers of conditioning. It seems like the kind of thing that would be a basis for how Autochthonian Castes and the Alchemical Exalted work; after all, aptitude is another thing that is part of that category. I certainly don't think there's any particular memory that serves as the basis for my attraction towards and aptitude for intellectual fields in general, and scientific ones in particular.<br /> <br /> A lot of what gives us a personality is emergent from things created by our genetics (not just neurology and muscle construction either, also the particulars of our hormone regulation). In other words, things we inherit from our parents. A lot of people notice similarities between parents and children, and that's not just confirmation bias. You don't have the actual memories of your parents, and yet there are evidently qualities that make you a continuation of that. There are people who draw meaning from that.<br /> <br /> I would think, in Creation, there could be people to draw meaning from a soul carrying traits between lives. Meaning from one those things are lost, seemingly forever, beneath the erasing darkness that seeps up from below the Underworld. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:54:05-07:00","id":893965,"title":"","content":"Very well-said, Isator! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've always disagreed with the notion that Lethe and Oblivion would be the same to the person experiencing it.<br /> <br /> To me, acknowledging the existence of a soul in the first place says there's something more to a person than memories and instincts and emotions and a sense of identity (even if the soul <i>houses</i> these things, that doesn't mean it's <i>only</i> these things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-19-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T06:59:01-07:00","id":893986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893237#post893237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without a doubt, the Lover as she is now. I have no interest to deal with her. She just feels like a congealed mass of bad and overused tropes. I feel like the old Abyssal idea preview made it abundantly clear she's a problem.<br /> <br /> If they do her a billion times better, well that could be ok. But as things are, nope. I can't think of anyone I know who used a very canon version of her well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one Abyssal I played used the canon version of her as his liege. Though he was expressly using her for contrast and to add some depth to her portrayal, as he was Chosen by her because he gave her a &quot;little brother&quot; figure. Candleflame of Hope Guttering on the Precipice of Oblivion was all about being &quot;too pure for this sinful world,&quot; or at least expressing that image: he was MEANT to make people care about him, see him as hope-filled and delightful and everything that makes the world worth preserving...and to constantly give the impression that there was nothing anybody could do to protect that, that it was hopeless, and thus the world's doom is all the more certain and fatalistic. In a sense, he is a contrast to the pursuit of pleasure-to-exhaustion that shows those who are far enough gone what they THOUGHT they were striving for...and realize now they have forever lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:03:36-07:00","id":894022,"title":"","content":"Isator, I like the idea that the hun soul may carry some of that from one incarnation to the next, but doesn't that mean that Oblivion (which is assumed to eliminate the hun forever) is quite different from Lethe (which reincarnates the hun) ? You seemed earlier to be saying it makes sense for them to be the same thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a question that probably doesn't merit a separate thread: Where did the idea come from that hun = higher soul, po = lower/animal soul, and one reincarnates while one sticks with the body?<br /> I know that it's based on the depiction of hun and p'o in Kindred of the East, and the words themselves are Chinese, but is this an actual belief in a Chinese religion, or a &quot;creative interpretation&quot; of a Chinese concept, or just kind of made up whole cloth for KotE?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:24:16-07:00","id":894033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894022#post894022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question that probably doesn't merit a separate thread: Where did the idea come from that hun = higher soul, po = lower/animal soul, and one reincarnates while one sticks with the body?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hun_and_po\" target=\"_blank\">Hun and po are real concepts in Chinese culture.</a> Some of the translations on that page suggest the idea that the po remains in the corpse while the hun goes on to the afterlife, although I don't know how reliable they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:29:27-07:00","id":894038,"title":"","content":"I believe there were also trends in Chinese spirituality which said that the hun was what could go on the Heaven, beyond worldly concerns, while the po descended to their idea analogous to the underworld, which was the subject of ancestral worship and offerings.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:30:51-07:00","id":894040,"title":"","content":"The Hun being the higher soul and the Po lower seems correct enough, though a human suppose to have 3 Hun and 7 Po, the Hun is also associated with Yang and the Po with Yin, each of them also have different names and jobs.<br /> <br /> Don't really read anything about Exalted's Underworld so that's all of the differences that I know going by forum discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:32:11-07:00","id":894043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894022#post894022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seemed earlier to be saying it makes sense for them to be the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was stating the position that I was going to present an argument against.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:59:24-07:00","id":894059,"title":"","content":"I'm of the position that finds Lethe as &quot;good&quot; to be a bit... questionable. Remember that it's for HUMAN souls generally, and the Primordials that created it weren't exactly that concerned with the well being or feelings of humanity. I mean, for all we know, it's the soul equivalent of processed meat. Soul goes in, is ground up and separated for recycling, then pressed into a fresh soul. That isn't exactly the nicest thing. The &quot;natural order&quot; isn't the same as good when it was created to the designs of alien titans. I mean, by that thought, the natural order would be no Exalted, enslaved gods, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:08:07-07:00","id":894070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894033#post894033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hun_and_po\" target=\"_blank\">Hun and po are real concepts in Chinese culture.</a> Some of the translations on that page suggest the idea that the po remains in the corpse while the hun goes on to the afterlife, although I don't know how reliable they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was interesting reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894043#post894043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was stating the position that I was going to present an argument against.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes more sense!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894059#post894059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the position that finds Lethe as &quot;good&quot; to be a bit... questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's definitely room for Abyssals or others to say &quot;Hey, you know what, the Underworld is a shitty place, but Lethe is shitty too. I vow to emancipate the souls of mankind from the tyranny of nature by making the Underworld into a true paradise where ancestors may be reunited with their descendants for all time.&quot; and then going about fundamentally altering the nature of the Underworld and human souls with necromantic and sorcerous workings... such as trying to make hun and po stay together in the Underworld so ghosts don't feel so incomplete.<br /> <br /> <br /> And of course, as with the disaster that created the Underworld and the Maw of Oblivion, there would be <b><i>so much</i></b> potential for mucking with the foundations of reality to backfire horribly. The Underworld could get <b><i>even worse</i></b>, or keeping the hun and po together in the Underworld might merely inflict the Shadow and Thorns problems from Wraith: the Oblivion upon dead people, making it even harder to resist Oblivion or find reincarnation...<br /> <br /> Or you could succeed with allowing hun and po to stay together with no unpleasant metaphysical side-effects... which then gradually brings about a new social order in the Underworld in which those who died before, and have no po, are relegated to second-class status or slavery or just soulforged because the Complete view the Incomplete as non-people...<br /> <br /> <br /> Because the universe may very well be unfair, but that doesn't mean humans know how to build a better one!<br /> <br /> Note: This isn't a philosophical statement against the concept of progress in the real world. I'm in favor of progress and believe in the great potential of humans to make our world and society vastly better than it is now. But I favor carefully thought-out progress with serious thought given to as many potential consequences as we can imagine. I see a robust tradition of speculative fiction, especially scifi, as a necessary part of this.<br /> <br /> Also I see the Underworld in Exalted as being almost as bleak as the World of Darkness, even though I prefer the rest of the setting to be much more optimsitic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:09:32-07:00","id":894073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894059#post894059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the position that finds Lethe as &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; to be a bit... questionable. Remember that it's for HUMAN souls generally, and the Primordials that created it weren't exactly that concerned with the well being or feelings of humanity. I mean, for all we know, it's the soul equivalent of processed meat. Soul goes in, is ground up and separated for recycling, then pressed into a fresh soul. That isn't exactly the nicest thing. The &amp;quot;natural order&amp;quot; isn't the same as good when it was created to the designs of alien titans. I mean, by that thought, the natural order would be no Exalted, enslaved gods, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that Oblivion is definitely complete soul destruction and Lethe is only erasure of memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:17:51-07:00","id":894078,"title":"","content":"It is also arguable that Lethe is an <i>incomplete</i> erasure of memories. Which is why reincarnation is meaningful; something of your prior lives' experiences remain. How much depends largely on plot for that specific character. I'd wager that more momentous lives weigh heavier, and that more ancient souls (as I believe canonically both Lethe's outgoing port and brand new creations are sources for higher souls) just have more that still lingers. So the ancient soul reincarnated will be wiser, or at least more experienced, with time. There would be something raw and fresh about truly new ones, as well, on their first lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:19:20-07:00","id":894080,"title":"","content":"We know that human souls permanently lose their memories upon reincarnation, while Dragon Kings can regain some past life memories. I wonder about the other races created by the Primordials -- were humans the only people to completely lose past life memories? Were Dragon Kings the only ones to retain past life memories? Were there several races that lost memories and several that kept them? Or did each race have a different way of reincarnating that's equally as alien as the Dragon Kings' nature?<br /> <br /> Then the question is whether it's good or bad that humans lose their past life memories. Dragon King society collapsed after the Primordial War, in part, because their society could not cope with the permanent loss of vast numbers of souls which the survivors else still remembered and had ties to. Their society was fundamentally not built to handle <i>death</i>. Past life memories and mate-bonds for Celestial Exalted are literal baggage that can bring traumatic memories of horrible events and unwanted social burdens or obligations, just as easily as they can bring useful memories or the inheritance of material or social wealth from a predecessor.<br /> <br /> If every human suddenly started having past life memories, societies everywhere would radically transform. Would they change for better, or for worse? Would humans be glad it had happened? Would they want it to change back, or want the loss of memory to be optional after each death? It would probably become a serious threat to the Immaculate dogma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:27:33-07:00","id":894086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894073#post894073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point is that Oblivion is definitely complete soul destruction and Lethe is only erasure of memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the point of view of a ghost, they're basically identical. Only real reason Lethe is considered the lesser of two evils is ecological. Too many souls fall to oblivion, Creation becomes depopulated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:29:20-07:00","id":894089,"title":"","content":"That depends entirely on their worldview. Viewing your memories, or even personality, as the most essential part of your selfhood is a specific cultural concept. Not everybody even on Earth believes that way. In Hinduism for example, continuity of selfhood happens through the reincarnating atman and its karma, even though memories are generally lost with each reincarnation. Buddhism denies that selfhood has any reality or genuine continuity even from one day to the next while we're still alive, no matter how we feel about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:34:08-07:00","id":894094,"title":"","content":"It's important for the cycle of reincarnation and the utter annihilation of the soul to be meaningfully distinct from each other, so that your compassionate Abyssal bodhisattva can preach sermons explaining how lethe is a scam and the true peace to be found in (little-o) oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:42:42-07:00","id":894102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893947#post893947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, just a thing that you particularly enjoy consuming because of its flavour.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat is the basis of favoured tastes? The series of synaptic responses that provoke a positive association with consuming a particular thing. The conditioned or genetically coded circuitry that connects the relevant parts of your brain?<br /> <br /> Is it memory? Is there an event in your life that you remember that makes a thing desirable to taste, that compels one particularly towards it? If you like the taste of fudge above all other sweets, would that cease to be the case even if you were made to forget what fudge even was?<br /> <br /> Do you have habits? Do you have emotional patterns? Consistent cognitive processes? Muscle memory?<br /> <br /> Things that largely arise from how chemicals and electrical impulses are shunted around the particular architecture of your brain?<br /> <br /> If you had no memories, a lot of that would remain. A lot of your impulses, what attracts and repels, how one responds, would remain consistent. You might not recognise anybody else, but there can be a fair amount by which others can recognise you.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the reincarnated soul might not be a seat for those patterns. That a person who lives long enough to see the same soul over multiple lifetimes exhibit many of the same traits that have little or nothing to do with procedural memory. Maybe continuously make the same positive contributions. Maybe gradually transition away from bad habits as altered environments add new layers of conditioning. It seems like the kind of thing that would be a basis for how Autochthonian Castes and the Alchemical Exalted work; after all, aptitude is another thing that is part of that category. I certainly don't think there's any particular memory that serves as the basis for my attraction towards and aptitude for intellectual fields in general, and scientific ones in particular.<br /> <br /> A lot of what gives us a personality is emergent from things created by our genetics (not just neurology and muscle construction either, also the particulars of our hormone regulation). In other words, things we inherit from our parents. A lot of people notice similarities between parents and children, and that's not just confirmation bias. You don't have the actual memories of your parents, and yet there are evidently qualities that make you a continuation of that. There are people who draw meaning from that.<br /> <br /> I would think, in Creation, there could be people to draw meaning from a soul carrying traits between lives. Meaning from one those things are lost, seemingly forever, beneath the erasing darkness that seeps up from below the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really put it in scientific terms, so much as the beliefs of certain reincarnation-based religio-philosophies, but that's essentially what I'd expect/want from the game/run as ST. The reincarnated soul won't remember anything, but will like similar things, have some similar personality traits, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:45:07-07:00","id":894104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894086#post894086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the point of view of a ghost, they're basically identical. Only real reason Lethe is considered the lesser of two evils is ecological. Too many souls fall to oblivion, Creation becomes depopulated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In one I die for ever. In the other I get amnesia.<br /> I'd rather get amnesia than die.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could see some people arguing there's no difference. But that's how I'd view it. And I think quite a lot of people in the world would prefer amnesia to death (including the many people in Asia who take comfort from the idea they'll reincarnate with no memories, and so clearly do view it differently to utter oblivion). More so in Creation where reincarnation-based religions are wide-spread, and oblivion-cults are viewed as heretical, so people will have heard plenty of propaganda telling them Lethe=good.<br /> <br /> Not to say that every ghost sees it that way: in fact, the people who stick around as ghosts for a long time are going to mostly be from the small minority of Creation-ites who do view Lethe as no better than Oblivion. A lot of ghosts won't though... but they're the ones who slip into Lethe after not too long a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-19-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:45:57-07:00","id":894106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894094#post894094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important for the cycle of reincarnation and the utter annihilation of the soul to be meaningfully distinct from each other, so that your compassionate Abyssal bodhisattva can preach sermons explaining how lethe is a scam and the true peace to be found in (little-o) oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of how Solars will argue that Abyssals are truly monstrous: they don't just kill people, they annihlate their souls.<br /> But there's that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:47:19-07:00","id":894109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=893920#post893920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;Lethe and Oblivion are equivalent&quot; thing is something that's been on my mind ever since I've read a few things that made me think about the nature of memory and personality and how they're not quite as equivalent as people have tended to suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much do you know about the game <i>SOMA</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:48:23-07:00","id":894110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894102#post894102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reincarnated soul won't remember anything, but will like similar things, have some similar personality traits, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is similar to how it works in the Wheel of Time: people generally don't remember past lives, but their personalities don't change much, or at all. I imagine that in Creation personalities would change more than in the Wheel of Time, and in general I don't believe that inborn nature predominates over nurture (socialization and life experiences)*, but to some extent the same principle makes sense for Creation, as Isator described.<br /> <br /> *Particularly not in the real world, but it wouldn't be verisimil to me if humans even in fantasy didn't have some significant contribution from both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:12:54-07:00","id":894135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894033#post894033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hun_and_po\" target=\"_blank\">Hun and po are real concepts in Chinese culture.</a> Some of the translations on that page suggest the idea that the po remains in the corpse while the hun goes on to the afterlife, although I don't know how reliable they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the Bible likewise makes a distinction between &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;spirit&quot; that generations of pastors have allowed to be forgotten.<br /> <br /> According to scripture, God formed man's body from dust, breathed spirit into the body, and the man became a soul.<br /> <br /> A person has a body and a spirit, but does not <i>have</i> a soul; a person <i>is</i> a soul. The soul is the consciousness and identity that arises from the combination of body and spirit. This is why the word &quot;soul&quot; is synonymous with &quot;person&quot;; &quot;five souls were lost at sea today&quot;.<br /> <br /> When a person dies, their spirit returns to God, their body returns to dust, and the soul (person) falls into Sheol (the metaphorical Grave; conceptual underworld) where there is no work, no pain, no understanding, no learning, and no worship. That is to say that death is a state of oblivion; a form of unconsciousness beyond mere sleep. God needs to rebuild the body and breath new life (spirit) into it before the soul can reawaken and experience continuity of consciousness and identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> One can see the Po soul which animates the body as roughly analogous to the animating breath of God, save that the Po soul remains with the body upon death instead of departing. The soul (consciousness/identity) of the person is analogus to the Hun soul, which figuratively descends into the Grave, though obviously the Underworld is very different from Sheol, which is more like a less permanent form of Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:57:14-07:00","id":894169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894089#post894089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Hinduism for example, continuity of selfhood happens through the reincarnating atman and its karma, even though memories are generally lost with each reincarnation. Buddhism denies that selfhood has any reality or genuine continuity even from one day to the next while we're still alive, no matter how we feel about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, somebody provides an answer to that question.<br /> <br /> I mean, I haven't asked it yet in this thread, but that was mostly out of a sense of futility.<br /> <br /> The point about a reincarnating atman and karma is particularly interesting to me, even if Exalted doesn't quite have the same concepts (I would find my notion of continuing cognitive patterns to be similar).<br /> <br /> Particularly considering that even if a ghost or living person or whatever thought strictly in terms of their continuing consciousness, is that the only thing to be concerned about leaving behind?<br /> <br /> There are people who do not believe anything of them will continue to exist when they die; does that mean that all states following the moment of their death are equivalent to them? Does that person not care about their legacy, the distribution of their possessions, the conditions of their loved ones, past the point where they think they will cease to exist?<br /> <br /> A person who thinks their own type of personality, their conditioned responses, all that jazz, contribute something positive to Creation might think in terms analogous to their reincarnated soul being something they bequeath back unto the world; something of themselves that they leave behind to do good again. Hell, not even the world; a person with particular self-esteem can think of it simply down to the person they'll be reborn as, that that person might get something out of inheriting them that they wouldn't from anybody else, or given a brand new soul.<br /> <br /> When you think about it, that's kind of what goes on behind the Immaculate Philosophies views on reincarnation; upright living continuously perfects you until you can be reborn Exalted, and make some <i>really</i> significant contributions.<br /> <br /> That's something beyond just &quot;there need to be enough souls available&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:03:04-07:00","id":894174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894106#post894106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more of how Solars will argue that Abyssals are truly monstrous: they don't just kill people, they annihlate their souls.<br /> But there's that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I GUESS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:54:51-07:00","id":894211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894106#post894106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more of how Solars will argue that Abyssals are truly monstrous: they don't just kill people, they annihlate their souls.<br /> But there's that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Abyssals, of course, call the Solars heartless for forcing poor ghosts into turn after turn through cruel samsara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:57:02-07:00","id":894214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894094#post894094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important for the cycle of reincarnation and the utter annihilation of the soul to be meaningfully distinct from each other, so that your compassionate Abyssal bodhisattva can preach sermons explaining how lethe is a scam and the true peace to be found in (little-o) oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAmusingly <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>, when I mentioned the Black Psychopomp (aka Walker in Darkness) above, that was basically his thing. He found meaning in the fact he had no memory. He saw purpose to it, and it was to show him the correct path so he could help others. BUT, not everyone is ready for that path, and for them Lethe is a necessary thing, so they can reach the point where they can willingly discard their memories and eventually existance.<br /> <br /> Was it horrifying? Oh hell yes. But he wasn't malicious about it. He wasn't trying to be pushy, he let people come to him, he wasn't trying to recruit (and discouraged that). Deathlords in that game had been very antagonistic, so meeting one who wasn't so was a bit discomforting. They expected a trap and fight when he asked for them to meet him, and instead they found a picnic in a Shadowland. It was creepy, but in part because he was a true believer yet didn't seem crazy so much as mistaken. So I really like you mentioning that. Obviously, it's something I played with.<br /> <br /> Also, the reason he wanted to meet them was this was a world where Abyssals weren't Deathlord created (so super non-canon) and he didn't understand them, but thought they might lead him to understanding he needed. Normally he dealt only with the dead, so it was an exception. *claping for Vance*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:54:28-07:00","id":894467,"title":"","content":"So, to change the subject completely (not that this isn't a good discussion).<br /> <br /> I was reading the Abyssal 3e preview the other day, and it was talking about how the ability trees are going to be based on the Deathlords (not sure how I feel about that, but that's neither here nor there).<br /> For example, Presence is based on the Lover (so full of seduction charms) while Resistance is based on the First and Forsaken Lion.<br /> This made me wonder: will there be 25 Deathlords written up? 12.5? Or will some Deathlords have 3 trees?<br /> Will the Deathlords be written to be the platonic ideals of particular charm trees (I mean, will the Bodhisvatta become not just a guy who lives on an island, but an active spooky sailor who sails around leading ghost ships)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:16:33-07:00","id":894474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894467#post894467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Presence is based on the Lover (so full of seduction charms)</div> </div> </div> </div>We saw <i>some</i> Presence Charms that nominally correspond to the Lover (and also mirror Solar Presence Charms that are also focused on seduction or enhancing appearance). That doesn't make it the whole tree.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs I recall what they've said of it, Deathlords will cover themes, that can encompass several Abilities, and there will be Abilities that can branch in the direction of several Deathlords.<br /> <br /> If it was a one to one basis, you'd wind up with a First and Forsaken Lion who inspires no Melee or War. Does that seem right to you?<br /> <br /> Look at the section on the Bishop, how it describes the kinds of Charms that derive from him.<br /> <br /> Is there no Presence there?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:57:50-07:00","id":894487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894104#post894104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say that every ghost sees it that way: in fact, the people who stick around as ghosts for a long time are going to mostly be from the small minority of Creation-ites who do view Lethe as no better than Oblivion. A lot of ghosts won't though... but they're the ones who slip into Lethe after not too long a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that ghosts don't have a conscious choice in whether they exist- either they have unfinished business or they don't. Your beliefs only influence how much business you consider important enough to stay for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:40:24-07:00","id":894510,"title":"","content":"That's partly true, but I don't think entirely: the Blessed Isle's Underworld was described as having a lot less ghosts than you'd expect for the population, because they've spent their whole lives being told they should reincarnate.<br /> <br /> There is a certain amount of choice in deciding whether your unfinished business matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:55:23-07:00","id":894518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894510#post894510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's partly true, but I don't think entirely: the Blessed Isle's Underworld was described as having a lot less ghosts than you'd expect for the population, because they've spent their whole lives being told they should reincarnate.<br /> <br /> There is a certain amount of choice in deciding whether your unfinished business matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are conditioned that their own lives don't matter, plus they have little to lve for. There are no important deeds they were even allowed to attempt, let alone dream of attaining. They are a spiritually broken people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:00:18-07:00","id":894519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894518#post894518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are conditioned that their own lives don't matter, plus they have little to lve for. There are no important deeds they were even allowed to attempt, let alone dream of attaining. They are a spiritually broken people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong, the wizard is right. Most DRAGON-BLOODED go straight to Lethe and rarely leave Ghosts, because they have been conditioned to just flow into reincarnation.<br /> <br /> That's why the Blessed Isle has nothing to do with its Underworld counterpart. If all DBs (who are not at all spiritually broken) became ghosts en masse, you'd have them overturning Stygia, or at least becoming a major problem, and this has never happened. And all of them are told they have all of the world to live for, and that they matter more for anything, more than anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 05-19-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:26:25-07:00","id":894530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894518#post894518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are conditioned that their own lives don't matter, plus they have little to lve for. There are no important deeds they were even allowed to attempt, let alone dream of attaining. They are a spiritually broken people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;spiritually broken&quot; is a bit of an exaggeration. Or rather, subjective. Most people in most of history accomplished no important deeds (I mean, on a large scale: they accomplished important deeds like raising their kids, being a good husband or wife, helping the people in their village, etc. But not anything of great significance to those outside their village). I'm not sure that makes them spiritually broken.<br /> Who's more spiritually broken: the medieval English peasant whose goal in life is to care for his family and farm, or the one who dreams of achieving mighty deeds and a high position in basically the only way a medieval English peasant might do so: by going to France and being really, really, really good at stabbing French people, and looting their stuff.<br /> Who's more spiritually broken: the modern man whose ambition in life is to look after his family shop, doing exactly what his parents did, or the ruthlessly ambitious guy who fights his way to CEO or President or whatever, not caring who he steps on on the way.<br /> <br /> Now, I do see where you're coming from, the Immaculate Order does massively push the &quot;know your place&quot; rhetoric, but I wouldn't say that makes them &quot;spiritually broken&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T01:32:49-07:00","id":894612,"title":"","content":"You're not spiritually broken if you don't want to be a hero.<br /> <br /> That makes you <b>sane.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:13:30-07:00","id":894726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894530#post894530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think &quot;spiritually broken&quot; is a bit of an exaggeration. Or rather, subjective. Most people in most of history accomplished no important deeds (I mean, on a large scale: they accomplished important deeds like raising their kids, being a good husband or wife, helping the people in their village, etc. But not anything of great significance to those outside their village). I'm not sure that makes them spiritually broken.<br /> Who's more spiritually broken: the medieval English peasant whose goal in life is to care for his family and farm, or the one who dreams of achieving mighty deeds and a high position in basically the only way a medieval English peasant might do so: by going to France and being really, really, really good at stabbing French people, and looting their stuff.<br /> Who's more spiritually broken: the modern man whose ambition in life is to look after his family shop, doing exactly what his parents did, or the ruthlessly ambitious guy who fights his way to CEO or President or whatever, not caring who he steps on on the way.<br /> <br /> Now, I do see where you're coming from, the Immaculate Order does massively push the &quot;know your place&quot; rhetoric, but I wouldn't say that makes them &quot;spiritually broken&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I get what they were going for. If it's still there, remember that on the Isle, DBs have been known to just... take land. Basically, they declare the people (I don't remember exactly so this is off memory) spiritually corrupt and therefore they can just &quot;save it&quot; by claiming it. You can do whatever you want to them with no consequences. In that case, you're going to hope and pray that either you reincarnate away from the Isle, or that you become a Dragon Blooded yourself and get to live the high life. It's not that they're broken in life, but that Lethe is their only hope of escaping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:12:42-07:00","id":894753,"title":"","content":"The Tomb Kings of Khemri were always my favourite fantasy undead faction because for the most part they're not actively malicious or trying to emulate their lives, inactive until someone's stupid enough to disturb their rest.<br /> <br /> If I had to do a dual kingdom in the Underworld I'd have the transition be less seasonal and more 'the stars are right' with the incumbent undead monarch being absolutely terrified of what their ancestor will make of a situation that\u2019s beyond their control but possibly willing to venture into their crypt as a nuclear option. This is not disimilar to how I portray Sijan's defensive situation, it's got a lot of potential military might tied up in a valley of kings that most invaders wouldn't be stupid enough to venture so a threat to the city might require the best negotiator the Mortician's Order has to put their life on the line to visit one of these tombs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:54:29-07:00","id":894779,"title":"","content":"I want this bike for my abyssal<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-82/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/WON82.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-82/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wielder of Names 5-82 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-82/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-82/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And then the usual. An underworld interesting enough to adventure in. A stygia that isn't a puppet of the Deathlods. Interesting places between the big necropoli. Something that makes Abyssals better at ruling the underworld than Solars would be. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:44:36-07:00","id":894812,"title":"","content":"All this talk about reincarnation and souls got me thinking. I hope the books are less absolute on what happens to souls in this edition. There are already references to reincarnation in the core, but I hope it's never spelled out whether its random or happens with some sort of judgement. I also hope its never made clear what happens to excess souls(as in, the population of creation in the first age was much larger than it is today, where are all those souls right now?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:46:21-07:00","id":894816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894812#post894812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where are all those souls right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the answer was &quot;they're all ghosts, that's why the Underworld is full of ghosts&quot; ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:49:56-07:00","id":894821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894816#post894816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the answer was &quot;they're all ghosts, that's why the Underworld is full of ghosts&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>What i understand is that ghosts happen when someone has unfinished matters that keep them tied to earth. It would be a little weird if some person died perfectly content but then became a ghost because whoops we dont have a body for you yet, gotta wait until someone has a baby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:56:50-07:00","id":894829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894821#post894821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i understand is that ghosts happen when someone has unfinished matters that keep them tied to earth. It would be a little weird if some person died perfectly content but then became a ghost because whoops we dont have a body for you yet, gotta wait until someone has a baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't those souls hang out in the Well of Souls? Or was that only an Autochthonian thing?<br /> <br /> [EDIT] Nevermind. You were saying you DON'T want it to be that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:21:10-07:00","id":894843,"title":"","content":"It could be interesting to leave it open to interpretation what happens between entering Lethe and getting reincarnated. Nobody remembers, so nobody knows! What exactly determines who gets reincarnated, and when, and into what life circumstances? It isn't at all likely that Lethe functions with any regard for human concepts of morality (Immaculate or otherwise), since it was made by Primordials... but are humans reincarnated in the order they died, so if you die in the Age of Sorrows you &quot;wait in line&quot; for millennia while people who died in the First Age go first? Is there any actual increasing enlightenment of hun over time? What, if anything, do hun experience while waiting, if they aren't ghosts? Somebody somewhere might believe that if the number of souls entering Lethe is larger than the human birthrate, the &quot;excess&quot; just go straight to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> And what happens to people who had their minds destroyed by Fair Folk (or Dragon-Blooded or Infernals with certain charms), when they die? Is their soul actually destroyed too, or perfectly healthy after reincarnation, or messed up so that it can't reincarnate and/or becomes an especially fucked up ghost, or reincarnates but with lasting damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:33:31-07:00","id":895007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894467#post894467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to change the subject completely (not that this isn't a good discussion).<br /> <br /> I was reading the Abyssal 3e preview the other day, and it was talking about how the ability trees are going to be based on the Deathlords (not sure how I feel about that, but that's neither here nor there).<br /> For example, Presence is based on the Lover (so full of seduction charms) while Resistance is based on the First and Forsaken Lion.<br /> This made me wonder: will there be 25 Deathlords written up? 12.5? Or will some Deathlords have 3 trees?<br /> Will the Deathlords be written to be the platonic ideals of particular charm trees (I mean, will the Bodhisvatta become not just a guy who lives on an island, but an active spooky sailor who sails around leading ghost ships)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meant to reply to this one but forgot. I won't deny I'm a bit hesitant about the Deathlord charm tree thing. It could end up making the Deathlords super, SUPER important the way they were in second ed. That said, I expect that other trees not based off them, but other Underworld entities of power would also exist. Ones based off one quarter of the Dual Monarchy, Hekatonkhire, or... heck, even super-powerful mysteries like the Kraken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894843#post894843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be interesting to leave it open to interpretation what happens between entering Lethe and getting reincarnated. Nobody remembers, so nobody knows! What exactly determines who gets reincarnated, and when, and into what life circumstances? It isn't at all likely that Lethe functions with any regard for human concepts of morality (Immaculate or otherwise), since it was made by Primordials... but are humans reincarnated in the order they died, so if you die in the Age of Sorrows you &quot;wait in line&quot; for millennia while people who died in the First Age go first? Is there any actual increasing enlightenment of hun over time? What, if anything, do hun experience while waiting, if they aren't ghosts? Somebody somewhere might believe that if the number of souls entering Lethe is larger than the human birthrate, the &quot;excess&quot; just go straight to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> And what happens to people who had their minds destroyed by Fair Folk (or Dragon-Blooded or Infernals with certain charms), when they die? Is their soul actually destroyed too, or perfectly healthy after reincarnation, or messed up so that it can't reincarnate and/or becomes an especially fucked up ghost, or reincarnates but with lasting damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these are exceptionally good questions, and as I've said before, we don't know FOR SURE why no one or thing comes back from Oblivion. It could even be not that it actually destroys them so much as going in means you'll never come out in Creation. Which... actually brings up an interesting idea. There are other realities out there, some sealed away. What if the reason no one returns is Oblivion is a one way door into them. At least for now. If enough things pass through, could the door open both ways?<br /> <br /> Considering the Well of Urd, it seems like that could be the case. And that could be an interesting story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:58:39-07:00","id":895075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894843#post894843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't at all likely that Lethe functions with any regard for human concepts of morality (Immaculate or otherwise), since it was made by Primordials...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Was</i> it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Who knows, might be that they found it out there somewhere in the Wyld and plugged it in, figuring, &quot;This looks good enough.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T21:11:48-07:00","id":895275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=894104#post894104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In one I die for ever. In the other I get amnesia.<br /> I'd rather get amnesia than die.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're either not around to remember your life, or you just don't remember. Either way, for that particular go-round, you're done.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (including the many people in Asia who take comfort from the idea they'll reincarnate with no memories </div> </div> </div>I'm only aware of buddhism, wherein Oblivion is basically the <i>goal. </i>Beyond all desire and suffering and knowing and needing to know and needing to..need. I dunno, wulf could probably explain the whole thing better than I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 05-21-2016, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T21:36:54-07:00","id":895286,"title":"","content":"I don't think Nirvana is quite the same as Oblivion, though I admit it sounds awfully similar.<br /> <br /> Certainly it is not the same in Zen, which includes the belief in finding Nirvana and existing in Nirvana while still alive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Revenge, your post quoted Wizard's wrong and part of Wizard's post isn't in a quote box so it looks like you're agreeing with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2016, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:19:33-07:00","id":895301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're either not around to remember your life, or you just don't remember. Either way, for that particular go-round, you're done. </div> </div> </div>What is &quot;me&quot;? Is it just my memories, or is it my soul? Because if it's my memories, does that mean I die a little bit every time I forget things? Did I even exist when I was 1, considering I have no memories of it? But if it's my soul, then amnesia is not death. It's just amnesia.<br /> <br /> When people have car accidents or whatever and get complete retrograde amnesia, as very occasionally happens, do their families consider them to have &quot;died&quot; or just suffer from a mental condition? I'd say very much the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm only aware of buddhism, wherein Oblivion is basically the <i>goal. </i>Beyond all desire and suffering and knowing and needing to know and needing to..need. I dunno, wulf could probably explain the whole thing better than I can. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but. Your average Buddhist peasant in Thailand isn't thinking &quot;one day I'll cease to exist entirely, like atheists believe they do&quot;, they're thinking &quot;I'll reincarnate continually, and eventually I'll ascend to ultimate bliss, and while I'm waiting the tens of thousands of years that'll take I'll donate to temples to make merit and get a good reincarnation&quot;. Not to mention afterlives of suffering/joy that go between lives in most .<br /> <br /> And many other reincarnationist religions/philosophies don't view identity the way Buddhism does. In Hinduism, the aim isn't to cease existing, but rather unite with the ultimate existence of God itself.<br /> This is the whole point of karma. I mean, if your next life was an entirely different person, why even worry about your karma? And that's certainly how Immaculates in Exalted view it.<br /> <br /> Although on the other hand, the Bishop's followers do think in a more Buddhist* way: Oblivion, non-existence, is bliss, while existence is suffering, and thus Oblivion is the ultimate goal.<br /> *As I said, I think Nirvana=Oblivion is a bit of a simplification, though it can be viewed that way.<br /> <br /> Anyway. My point is that people in Exalted will have different views, but generally they're going to view Lethe as positive and Oblivion as negative. Occasionally it will be the other way round, or they'll view them as functionally the same. I could definitely see some philosophers arguing that Lethe is functionally identical to Lethe (before Immaculates beat them up), but as there are millions of people in Asia very concerned with what will happen to them in their next life, I'm pretty confident that it's not going to be a popular idea in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-21-2016, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T23:33:30-07:00","id":895339,"title":"","content":"Buddhist Nirvana isn't Oblivion at all.<br /> <br /> Superficially, there are similarities: a soul that is destroyed is beyond suffering, and eliminating suffering is the goal.<br /> <br /> But according to Skandha theory, even if you had a soul that could be touched, that could be manipulated, with every single memory encased within like a piece of amber, it still isn't proof that there is a self at all, because not even normal, breathing people have selves that are consistent from moment to moment. Impermanence affects everything.<br /> <br /> Nirvana, then, is the state that is beyond life, beyond death, beyond joy and suffering, something that cannot be changed. &quot;Nirvana&quot; means &quot;extinguish&quot; and to some, it's the blowing out of the dim light of the illusion of self to enter the sun-like radiance of Nirvana. To me, Nirvana is the blowing out of the light to realize the darkness that has always been there, just out of reach. To some, it's a state of pure bliss, but to me, it's probably something beyond even that.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Neverborn seek Oblivion because they want to be free only of suffering, and want to stop existing entirely; they want to annihilate themselves. Buddhists seek Awakening to attain Nirvana at some point, to be free of both suffering <b>and</b> joy, in a state beyond both annihilation and existence.<br /> <br /> Also, another thing that states that Nirvana isn't Oblivion: the Buddha attained Nirvana, and gained multiple supernatural powers in the process. The Neverborn's power is not borne of Oblivion, as they have not entered it: those powers are just merely in service of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T23:44:42-07:00","id":895345,"title":"","content":"Every time the Oblivion = Nirvana comparison come up, here's what in my mind:<br /> <br /> European: &quot;Hey, those redskin all have a deity who is a coyote, they MUST be the same god!&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T01:33:49-07:00","id":895380,"title":"","content":"There is that.<br /> I recently tried to explain the differences between Catholics, Anglicans and Baptists to my Chinese boss, who wanted her students to read an English extract which briefly mentioned them to her students. Not easy. After 10 minutes I just went with &quot;they're all Christians but they have different leaders&quot; which is rather reductive.<br /> <br /> Also, most Westerners assume that Buddhists are like Buddhists in the West, whom I've found to be generally rather different to Buddhists in China and Thailand (and I assume Tibet, Vietnam, etc). And of course, those themselves are quite different from each other, what with Mahayana, Zen, Theravada, Pure Land, etc (whose differences I don't really understand, but they presumably are different), not to mention the interpretations of different cultures. Chinese and Thai Buddhism certainly seemed different to me.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into actual different religions like Sikhs, Hindus and Jains, as you say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-21-2016, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T04:50:27-07:00","id":895421,"title":"","content":"If anything, seems more like &quot;Hey, is this Nirvana like our idea of Heaven, or not? I think it is because...&quot; (because Oblivion is sort of a concept made up the Exalted fanbase, not something from another culture) followed up by another person going &quot;Now I'm don't care about this Nirvana stuff, but *that's* what you think of Heaven? Theologically I cannot agree with this and we need to talk about this.&quot;, because pretty much no one actually agrees about what these apparently basic beliefs are, even within a culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:38:56-07:00","id":895713,"title":"","content":"Whereas us Taoists would very much prefer existing outside Fate to not existing at all<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:02:53-07:00","id":896291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=895380#post895380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is that.<br /> I recently tried to explain the differences between Catholics, Anglicans and Baptists to my Chinese boss, who wanted her students to read an English extract which briefly mentioned them to her students. Not easy. After 10 minutes I just went with &quot;they're all Christians but they have different leaders&quot; which is rather reductive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, I couldn't tell you the difference between Anglicans and Baptists, and I <i>am</i> Baptist. If I had to guess, something about baptism by immersion, <i>probably</i>?<br /> Really, we all like to harp on &quot;of the Dragons or from the Dragons&quot; (at least, I do), but RL sectarian differences can be exactly that obscure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:09:48-07:00","id":896428,"title":"","content":"I can explain it if you're interested. Not really much to do with Exalted though.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Baptists don't allow Christenings, only adult baptism, while Anglican do Christenings and adult baptisms. A lot of stricter Baptists believe in predestination, but the Anglican church is firmly in the camp of Ariminianism (ie there's no predestination). Baptists believe that the bread and wine are only metaphorical representations of Christ's body and blood. Anglicans... have a very vague position in order to let people of both opinions fit into the Church.<br /> Anglicans believe in apostolic succession of bishops and priests, Baptists believe all Christians are priests. Anglicans have a hierarchy of vicars/bishops/archbishops, Baptists do not. Anglican vicars are appointed by the hierarchy, Baptists vote for their pastors. Anglicans didn't allow women to be vicars/bishops until relatively recently, Baptists have I think allowed it for longer, though I'm not sure (I've never seen/met a female Baptist pastor, but I don't remember it being explicitly banned). There are also stylistic differences, with Anglicans having a more formalised liturgy, but that's not a theological thing. Anglicans include a wider strand than Baptists, so an Anglican church could be evangelical or virtually Catholic, while Baptist churches are less so.<br /> So... yeah, in most ways the differences aren't that big. I guess the most significant things are probably the organisation of it. Certainly, as someone baptised in a Baptist church, I feel no issue going to an Anglican church the way I would a Mormon church, though Christenings make me a bit uncomfortable. Certainly that kind of thing is far less important to me than avoiding homophobic or Creationist preachers. Hey, I go to a Church under the iron contol of the Communist party (The Three-Self Patriotic Movement, formerly the Three-Self Support Korea Oppose America Patriotic Movement, the only legal Protestant Church in China), and there's not much difference with western Churches.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-22-2016, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T19:01:38-07:00","id":896453,"title":"","content":"Extra Credits also has at least three &quot;Extra History&quot; videos up regarding Early Christian Schisms. I plan to watch them eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-22-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:34:17-07:00","id":900013,"title":"","content":"Pursuant to ghosts being treated as real people, making soulsteel out of ghosts should still be considered a heinous crime. Or, perhaps, MORE of a heinous crime than it was in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> And a good way to do that would be if Abyssals are like Solars in that they can draw Evocations out of any magical material, so that they never use soulsteel except as a very deliberate choice.<br /> <br /> This would also help move Abyssals away from &quot;destroyers of the world or struggling to NOT be a destroyer of the world; no other options!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:08:18-07:00","id":900031,"title":"","content":"Considering the abyssals are going to get bonuses for using the trappings of death...they might be able to use all magical materials like Solars but probably with some penalties since essentially if you aren't embracing your death knight look (guessing soulsteel and black jade at least look the part), you suffer in creation at least. At least that how it was in the abyssal preview in 2013, who knows what will happen by the time they come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:12:47-07:00","id":900035,"title":"","content":"A trapping of death is wearing perfume that people would normally only use to mask the scent of a corpse's decay.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean the perfume has to be made with the last tears of an orphan who was tortured to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:15:21-07:00","id":900039,"title":"","content":"Yeah it could be case but trappings of death might vary from table to table, I guess depending on what a ST and players agree on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:20:38-07:00","id":900042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900039#post900039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it could be case but trappings of death might vary from table to table, I guess depending on what a ST and players agree on.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many cultures do you think dress up their dead with the remains of OTHER dead people?<br /> <br /> What we're debating is whether or not soulsteel is more of a &quot;trapping of death&quot; than other magical materials, and I'm saying that you're focusing too much on what the Abyssal's armor and sword are made of and not enough on the fact that he's carrying armor and a sword.<br /> <br /> To that end, trappings of death involve how a culture treats the armor and swords of the death. If a culture paints the armor black or draps a black tabard over it, then the Abyssal needs to do the same, but he doesn't need to change which armor he wears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:28:26-07:00","id":900051,"title":"","content":"Not many cultures but there are a few, especially in creation there is probably quite a few, I mean death cults are relatively popular.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with that, but mostly saying to consider that we don't know yet what the rules are going to be for Abyssals and magical materials connection and wouldn't be surprised, if they get more bonuses of using soulsteel than other magical materials. Being limited in magical material use is not really a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:32:46-07:00","id":900058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900042#post900042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many cultures do you think dress up their dead with the remains of OTHER dead people?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some cultures sacrifice the spouses and slaves of the deceased and bury them with the corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:48:33-07:00","id":900083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900013#post900013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pursuant to ghosts being treated as real people, making soulsteel out of ghosts should still be considered a heinous crime. Or, perhaps, MORE of a heinous crime than it was in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> And a good way to do that would be if Abyssals are like Solars in that they can draw Evocations out of any magical material, so that they never use soulsteel except as a very deliberate choice.<br /> <br /> This would also help move Abyssals away from &quot;destroyers of the world or struggling to NOT be a destroyer of the world; no other options!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like this. Creation is a Bronze Age world where slavery and human sacrifice are not uncommon. Human lives aren't valued in the same way that they are in modern society and the idea of inherent human rights would be laughed at. Torture and mutilation are more common criminal punishments than long-term imprisonment and no one cares if a method of execution causes the condemned excessive pain - they'd probably count it as a bonus.<br /> <br /> For Abyssals to look at a piece of black metal filled with the tortured souls of the dead and go &quot;I, on moral grounds, will not use this&quot; is incongruous with the rest of the setting. Exceptions might exist, but turning down incredible power just because it causes someone else suffering is not a Bronze Age attitude.<br /> <br /> As a further point, how much humanity is left to ghosts is still up in the air and could potentially vary. From what I know of the Wraith setting, ghosts there are sometimes Drones, ghosts so broken that they go through the motions of their life and/or death and have essentially lost their ability of self-determination. In Wraith, Drones are often soulforged just to keep them from strengthening Oblivion in the end and because they are pretty much useless for anything else. If Drones become a thing in Exalted, you suddenly have a layer of moral ambiguity to soulsteel. You have these souls which are so broken it could be argued that they are no longer a person in any metaphysical sense. Would soulsteel forged from drones be considered something evil or would it be considered like a pound of hamburger at the grocery store?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:29:41-07:00","id":900126,"title":"","content":"Personally I would still be opposed to soulforging anything that's capable of feeling pain or suffering, just as I'm opposed to torturing kittens to death.<br /> <br /> But broadly, yes, this is a setting full of slavery and torture and genocide and other things many folks today consider atrocities or crimes against humanity. In the Realm, those are all Tuesday. In a lot of other cultures, they're probably just as blase or eager about these things. That isn't to say that characters can't be more compassionate... but I doubt the norm is to regard soulforging as wrong on the grounds that it hurts somebody.<br /> <br /> Now, if somebody finds out that their own ancestor was soulforged, that's different, because the victim was one of their in-group. And it may be that in Sijan all soulforging is despised. I imagine that necromancy is widely despised for being unholy (in actuality or in superstition), and for disturbing ancestors. But then again, some other culture might regard a necromancer who uses their spells to be a medium of the dead to be a holy person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-26-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:27:46-07:00","id":900251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900126#post900126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would still be opposed to soulforging anything that's capable of feeling pain or suffering, just as I'm opposed to torturing kittens to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soulforging produces super metal. Torturing kittens just produces dead kittens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:32:42-07:00","id":900258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900251#post900251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soulforging produces super metal. Torturing kittens just produces dead kittens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if I could somehow forge an incredibly badass gun from the corpses of tortured kittens, I would be morally opposed. The ends, I feel, do not justify the means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:45:45-07:00","id":900269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900083#post900083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't like the idea that Abyssals can use anything but soulsteel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:03:58-07:00","id":900281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900258#post900258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if I could somehow forge an incredibly badass gun from the corpses of tortured kittens, I would be morally opposed. The ends, I feel, do not justify the means.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine for you, but I guarantee that every military in the world would be hard at work churning out Screaming Cat Cannons or whatever they'd be called. And that's here in the modern day, not back in 1000 B.C.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900269#post900269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't like the idea that Abyssals can use anything but soulsteel?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that Abyssals would be, as a group, reluctant to use soulsteel when it is relatively easy to obtain in the Underworld and resonates with their powers most easily does not fit with the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:06:28-07:00","id":900282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900251#post900251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soulforging produces super metal. Torturing kittens just produces dead kittens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that the use of Soulforged Soulsteel in the Underworld is treated similarly to the use of Starmetal reforged from deities in Yu-Shan: with cautious disgust. I doubt the ghosts themselves are particularly comfortable around Deathknights with particularly well stocked panoplies. It'd be like walking into a house filled with lots of taxidermy, in that you'd start to wonder about the owner's attitudes toward other living things. I guess if you wanted to avoid that discussion, you could take the time, in game or during character creation, to source naturally occurring Soulsteel, from deeper in the Underworld, much like you could source Starmetal from meteor strikes in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:10:20-07:00","id":900286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900281#post900281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine for you, but I guarantee that every military in the world would be hard at work churning out Screaming Cat Cannons or whatever they'd be called. And that's here in the modern day, not back in 1000 B.C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because a bunch of people do or are willing to do a thing doesn't make that thing right. The discussion isn't about whether or not people would do it - obviously they would. It's about whether or not that thing is horrible, and obviously it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:42:32-07:00","id":900316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900281#post900281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Abyssals would be, as a group, reluctant to use soulsteel</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you go back and read my post again, you will not find me saying that.<br /> <br /> I said that if Abyssal Exalted had options outside of using soulsteel, then using soulsteel would be a deliberate choice, because it wouldn't be their only real option for powerful weapons.<br /> <br /> The context of my first paragraph is speaking meta-textually, of the books that present the world to us. The books that present ghosts as people and the question of soulsteel as a real moral compromise. As opposed to how the Infernal manual practically went out of its way to encourage us to view demons as raw materials for infernal artifacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> when it is relatively easy to obtain in the Underworld </div> </div> </div>A fair point, except not all Abyssals take the Second Breath in the Underworld or spend most of their time in the Underworld, and Deathlords with Abyssals will often be interest in expanding their influence into the living world.<br /> <br /> Abyssals would also have as much reason to raid the tombs of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and resonates with their powers most easily does not fit with the setting. </div> </div> </div>Orichalcum doesn't resonate most easily with the Solar Exalted. It's just that they're the ONLY ones for whom it resonates.<br /> <br /> And the entire question is whether Abyssal Exalted should only be able to resonate with soulsteel, or whether they can or should have options outside of soulsteel. Do you have any reason WHY Abyssals should not be able to resonate with jade, moonsilver, or starmetal?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-26-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:34:34-07:00","id":900414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900282#post900282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that the use of Soulforged Soulsteel in the Underworld is treated similarly to the use of Starmetal reforged from deities in Yu-Shan: with cautious disgust. I doubt the ghosts themselves are particularly comfortable around Deathknights with particularly well stocked panoplies. It'd be like walking into a house filled with lots of taxidermy, in that you'd start to wonder about the owner's attitudes toward other living things. I guess if you wanted to avoid that discussion, you could take the time, in game or during character creation, to source naturally occurring Soulsteel, from deeper in the Underworld, much like you could source Starmetal from meteor strikes in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Starmetal is going to just be fallen stars now and have nothing to do with dead gods. Personally, I'd expect that soulsteel would get treated much like slavery - taken as a fact of life (or death).<br /> <br /> Also, I've been in houses full of taxidermy. It just comes off as someone being proud of their hunting trophies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900286#post900286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because a bunch of people do or are willing to do a thing doesn't make that thing right. The discussion isn't about whether or not people would do it - obviously they would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you got my point. The setting shouldn't portray soulsteel as a shunned material when it has chattel slavery, drug cartels, human sacrifice, and casual prostitution represented in their Bronze Age contexts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/868227-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-underworld-abyssals-etc?p=900316#post900316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you go back and read my post again, you will not find me saying that.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The context of my first paragraph is speaking meta-textually, of the books that present the world to us. The books that present ghosts as people and the question of soulsteel as a real moral compromise. </div> </div> </div>Soulsteel isn't a moral compromise - it's a Faustian bargain in metallic form. In return for doing something terrible to another sapient being, you get power. Calling it a moral compromise implies that you have two goods which are in competition and you are attempting to satisfy both as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As opposed to how the Infernal manual practically went out of its way to encourage us to view demons as raw materials for infernal artifacts. </div> </div> </div>That was fine for First Circle Demons - it's the attitude that Hell itself has towards Demons of the First Circle. They are disposable, replaceable, and plentiful - why not use them as such? Conveying that casual disregard for sapient life was a big part of making Hell into Hell and I thought it was conveyed well without being explicit.<br /> <br /> It wasn't, however, appropriate for Demons of the Second Circle. Those are too unique to be reduced to a component in your next artifact so casually and also the most capable of opposing such treatment for themselves. But then that's part of what you already meant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the entire question is whether Abyssal Exalted should only be able to resonate with soulsteel, or whether they can or should have options outside of soulsteel. Do you have any reason WHY Abyssals should not be able to resonate with jade, moonsilver, or starmetal? </div> </div> </div>Yes. You are suggesting something that would divorce the Abyssal Exalted from their melodrama. Hard decisions, painful sacrifice, damning one's self for power - these are all part of the Abyssal thematic space. Abyssals should not get to take an easy way out and go jack the grave of a long dead Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:57:52-07:00","id":900471,"title":"","content":"If the Void ceases to be a distinct physical thing then becoming Soulsteel could be embraced by Spectres as the closest thing possible to ceasing to exist or the way to escape endless reincarnation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:06:31-07:00","id":900482,"title":"","content":"Or at least by some of them. I imagine guys driven insane by the treacherous seas of the Underworld might not all have similar viewpoints. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}